E["item:corrupted-brain-stem"] = {t="item",n="Corrupted Brain Stem",z="blackfathom",s="Corrupted Brain Stems are biological specimens harvested from the twisted naga and satyrs inhabiting Blackfathom Deeps and the Ashenvale coastline. Gershala Nightwhisper of Auberdine seeks them to study the physical deformities wrought by reckless magical corruption. By examining these brains, night elf scholars hope to understand and potentially prevent a similar fate from befalling the blood elves.",h="Corrupted Brain Stems are biological specimens harvested from the twisted naga and satyrs inhabiting...",sec={{t="Anatomy of Transformation",b="The satyrs and naga of Kalimdor stand as living testaments to the warping power of forbidden magic and demonic pacts. Long ago, reckless kaldorei highborne were irrevocably transformed into serpent-like aquatic beasts and demonic horned fiends. The brain stems harvested from these creatures exhibit heavy physical mutation, providing direct anatomical proof of how deep corruptive energies burrow into the nervous systems of once-elven beings.",sp=0},{t="Gershala's Warning",b="In the coastal settlement of Auberdine, the night elf Gershala Nightwhisper observes the troubling rumors surrounding the blood elves of the Eastern Kingdoms. Fearing that their flirtation with demonic sorcery will spawn yet another generation of monsters on Azeroth, Gershala tasks adventurers with venturing into Blackfathom Deeps. By dissecting both naga and satyr tissues, the researcher hopes to map the path of magical degeneration before another elven culture is lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield a Corrupted Brain Stem?",a="They are gathered from naga and satyrs residing within Blackfathom Deeps and along the surrounding shores of Ashenvale, including Blackfathom oracles, sea witches, and Fallenroot satyrs.",al={"who drops brain stems","corrupted brain stem drop","where to get brain stems"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these brain stems and why?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper, stationed in the Darkshore port of Auberdine, requests them to conduct anatomical research on magical corruption.",al={"who needs corrupted brain stem","gershala quest","turn in brain stems"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are night elves hoping to learn from these specimens?",a="Gershala fears that the blood elves' use of demonic magic will transform them into monsters, much like the ancient highborne became naga and satyrs. Studying these stems helps identify how demonic energies alter elven biology.",al={"why study naga satyr","researching the corruption lore","blood elf connection"},it="purpose"},{q="Can these be found outside of the Blackfathom Deeps caverns?",a="Yes. Certain Fallenroot satyrs and Blackfathom tide priestesses lingering outside the cavern entrance along the Ashenvale coast also carry them.",al={"outside blackfathom","ashenvale brain stems","do surface mobs drop them"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Corrupted Brain Stem?",a="A Corrupted Brain Stem is an anatomical specimen harvested from the satyrs and naga dwelling within and around Blackfathom Deeps. Both races were once night elves whose bodies and minds were violently altered by demonic pacts or ancient, shadowy depths. These brain stems carry the physical hallmarks of that magical deformation, making them valuable anatomical subjects for scholars studying how dark sorcery twists mortal flesh.",al={"what is corrupted brain stem","corrupted brain stem item","corrupted brainstem lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Corrupted Brain Stem come from?",a="These brain stems are taken from the Fallenroot satyrs and Blackfathom naga inhabiting the subterranean grottos and ruins around Blackfathom Deeps along the Ashenvale coast. Rather than being manufactured items, they are biological remnants of creatures warped over millennia by corruption, fel power, and dark transformations.",al={"where do corrupted brain stems come from","who drops corrupted brain stem","corrupted brain stem origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, collecting these remains is a grim reminder of their people's tragic history and the monstrous results of unchecked arcane and fel meddling.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts sent into Ashenvale brave the depths of Blackfathom to aid Auberdine's scholars in understanding the burgeoning threats across Azeroth."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackfathom deeps","corrupted brain stem","gershala nightwhisper","naga","researching the corruption","satyr"},rel={"quest:1275","npc:gershala-nightwhisper","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","subzone:auberdine","npc:lady-sarevess","topic:naga","topic:satyr"},src={"Corrupted Brain Stem","Researching the Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["item:fathom-core"] = {t="item",n="Fathom Core",z="blackfathom",s="The Fathom Core is a specialized relic recovered from a submerged fathom stone in the depths of Blackfathom Deeps. When deciphered, it provides a comprehensive record of elemental activity in the surrounding region. The Earthen Ring seeks this artifact to discern what dark rituals the Twilight's Hammer cult is conducting beneath Ashenvale.",h="The Fathom Core is a specialized relic recovered from a submerged fathom stone in the depths of Blackfathom...",sec={{t="Elemental Chronicle",b="Resting within an ancient fathom stone submerged among the Moonshrine Ruins, the Fathom Core serves as a historical record for elemental phenomena. It registers and preserves shifts, disruptions, and surges in the elements over time. For the shaman of the Earthen Ring stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost, acquiring the core is essential for understanding how the Twilight's Hammer cultists are manipulating the regional elements to serve their own ends.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fathom Core?",a="The Fathom Core is a magical device capable of recording and relating a detailed history of all elemental activity in its vicinity. It is found housed inside an ancient fathom stone within the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"what does fathom core do","fathom core lore","what is it"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Fathom Core located?",a="The core is located deep within the cavernous halls of Blackfathom Deeps on the Ashenvale coast. It sits enclosed inside a fathom stone resting under the waters of the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"fathom core location","where to find fathom core","fathom stone location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Fathom Core and why?",a="Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost, seeks the core. By analyzing its record of elemental shifts, Je'neu and his circle hope to decipher and counteract the subversive activities of the Twilight's Hammer cult inside the ruins.",al={"who needs fathom core","why does je'neu want fathom core","earthen ring fathom core"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The cultists have taken up residence in the submerged ruins to coerce and corrupt the local elements, seeking to bend them toward dark purposes and claim total control of the subterranean temple.",al={"twilight's hammer blackfathom","cultists in bfd"},it="motive"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As an artifact chronicling elemental currents, the Fathom Core is of immense interest to the Earthen Ring, demonstrating how ancient relics can reveal elemental manipulation.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the core directly aids Je'neu Sancrea and secures the Horde's foothold at Zoram'gar Outpost against the corruptive designs of the Twilight's Hammer."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"quest:6921","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"Fathom Core","Amongst the Ruins (Classic)"}}
E["item:head-of-kelris"] = {t="item",n="Head of Kelris",z="blackfathom",s="The severed head of Twilight Lord Kelris serves as undeniable proof that the leader of the Twilight's Hammer within Blackfathom Deeps has fallen. Carried out from the corrupted temple ruins, it is sought by representatives of the Argent Dawn to confirm the end of his profane ritual sacrifices.",h="The severed head of Twilight Lord Kelris serves as undeniable proof that the leader of the Twilight's Hammer...",sec={{t="A Trophy of Ruin",b="Within the submerged depths of the sunken Temple of Elune, Twilight Lord Kelris orchestrated dark sacrifices to Aku'mai, a monstrous pet of the Old Gods. Claiming his head marks the end of his tyrannical leadership over the Twilight's Hammer cultists and their naga allies in the cavern. The grisly trophy must be carried back to surface civilizations to assure leaders that Kelris's bloody ceremonies have finally ceased.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Dawn",b="For months, Kelris was presumed dead or lost by the Argent Dawn, only for his sinister influence to resurface alongside Kalimdor's encroaching shadows. When presented to agents in Darnassus or Thunder Bluff, the head settles lingering bounties and confirms that his attempts to plunge the world back into primeval chaos have been thwarted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Kelris was the leader of the Twilight's Hammer sect entrenched within Blackfathom Deeps. Allied with the naga, he orchestrated ritual sacrifices of innocents to feed Aku'mai, a hydra servant of an Old God, in pursuit of dark power and ancient chaos.",al={"who is kelris","kelris lore","twilight lord kelris"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Head of Kelris?",a="Alliance champions deliver the head to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus, while Horde adventurers bring it to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Dawnwatcher Selgorm serves the Argent Dawn, while Bashana Runetotem belongs to the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who takes kelris head","head of kelris turn in","who do i give kelris head to"},it="wants"},{q="Why does the Argent Dawn care about Kelris?",a="The Argent Dawn tracks malevolent threats that endanger Azeroth. Kelris was a known villain who had long eluded them, and his worship of the Old Gods and sacrifice of innocents posed a dire threat to the balance of Kalimdor.",al={"why argent dawn kelris","argent dawn blackfathom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the head obtained?",a="It is severed from the corpse of Twilight Lord Kelris inside his sanctum within the Blackfathom Deeps dungeon, located beneath the Zoram Strand along the coast of Ashenvale.",al={"where to get kelris head","kelris head location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Kelris?",a="It is the severed head of Twilight Lord Kelris, the leader of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who took root deep within the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. It serves as gruesome, undeniable proof that the cult's sinister master in the sunken temple has been slain and his rituals brought to an end.",al={"head of kelris","what is head of kelris","kelris head item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Head of Kelris come from?",a="The head is taken directly from Twilight Lord Kelris in the depths of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand. You must fight your way past his fanatical cultists and aberrant servants to slay the twilight lord in his inner sanctum before claiming it.",al={"where to get head of kelris","head of kelris origin","how to get head of kelris"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Delivering Kelris's head to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus avenges the desecration of an ancient night elf temple dedicated to Elune.",["faction:Horde"]="Presenting the head to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff earns the trust of the Cenarion Circle, proving their dedication to cleansing Kalimdor's corruption."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","bashana runetotem","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","head of kelris","selgorm","twilight lord kelris"},rel={"npc:twilight-lord-kelris","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:argent-dawn","npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm","npc:bashana-runetotem","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Head of Kelris","Blackfathom Villainy (Alliance)","Blackfathom Villainy (Horde)"}}
E["item:lorgalis-manuscript"] = {t="item",n="Lorgalis Manuscript",z="blackfathom",s="The Lorgalis Manuscript is an ancient text tied to the worship and lore of the Old Gods, preserved from the fallen night elven ruins beneath Ashenvale. Hidden within the sunken temple complex of Blackfathom Deeps, it holds secrets coveted by dark scholars seeking to awaken ancient, slumbering powers.",h="The Lorgalis Manuscript is an ancient text tied to the worship and lore of the Old Gods, preserved from the...",sec={{t="A Tome of Those Who Sleep",b="Dating back to the grand elven temples that stood before the Great Sundering, the Lorgalis Manuscript survived the cataclysmic flooding that submerged the ruins of Blackfathom. While the elves of antiquity gathered deep secrets, parts of their archives recorded darker powers. The manuscript contains potent lore tied directly to the Old Gods—knowledge said to open mystical doorways and stir ancient entities that sleep deep beneath the world. Stored away in a pitted iron chest amidst the flooded corridors, it has drawn the attention of cultists and shadow scholars alike.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="In the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge, an eccentric collector named Gerrig Bonegrip actively hires intrepid adventurers to venture across the sea to retrieve the text. Bonegrip speaks reverently of the 'end days' and the awakening of sleeping deities. Once recovered, the text is intended to be transcribed and shared among his shadowy circle of brothers and sisters, spreading forbidden insights that surface folk were never meant to comprehend.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="It is an ancient elven text containing dark, esoteric knowledge regarding the Old Gods. Its contents are said to hold the secrets necessary to unlock doorways and awaken slumbering primordial entities.",al={"what is lorgalis manuscript","lorgalis book lore","what does the manuscript do"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the manuscript located?",a="The manuscript rests within a pitted iron chest submerged deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, a ruined night elven temple located along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale.",al={"where to find lorgalis manuscript","manuscript location","blackfathom chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the manuscript?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip, an enigmatic lorekeeper operating out of the Forlorn Cavern in Ironforge, commissions adventurers to recover it. He plans to copy and distribute its ancient teachings among his secretive peers.",al={"who wants lorgalis manuscript","gerrig bonegrip quest","who is bonegrip"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Gerrig Bonegrip talk about the end days?",a="Bonegrip aligns himself with those who study and revere the Old Gods. His interest in ancient elven writings is focused on lore capable of awakening 'Those Who Sleep,' heralding what he considers the coming end times.",al={"gerrig end days","bonegrip cultist","bonegrip old gods"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the Lorgalis Manuscript come from, and who made it?",a="The manuscript originates from the ancient night elves who once inhabited the temple complex that has now sunk into Blackfathom Deeps. Long before the Sundering broke their city and submerged it beneath Ashenvale's waters, these long-dead elves recorded forbidden lore concerning cosmic entities and Those Who Sleep, locking the dangerous text within a pitted iron chest.",al={"lorgalis manuscript origin","who wrote lorgalis manuscript","where was lorgalis manuscript made"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The manuscript represents a rare bridge between ancient elven arcane lore and forbidden entities of the deep, offering insights coveted by those who traffic in dark arts.",["race:NightElf"]="The text was penned by ancient night elven ancestors before their temple sank beneath the waves, though its obsession with slumbering dark powers makes it a tragic relic of their civilization's past."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","ironforge","lorgalis","manuscript","old god","those who sleep"},rel={"quest:971","npc:gerrig-bonegrip","zone:blackfathom","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ashenvale","zone:ironforge","topic:old-god"},src={"Lorgalis Manuscript","Knowledge in the Deeps (Classic)"}}
E["item:sapphire-of-aku-mai"] = {t="item",n="Sapphire of Aku'Mai",z="blackfathom",s="Sapphires of Aku'Mai are glowing, water-infused mineral clusters growing along the subterranean tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps. The encroaching naga have begun harvesting these gems, prompting the Earthen Ring to seek them out before their potent arcane power can be exploited.",h="Sapphires of Aku'Mai are glowing, water-infused mineral clusters growing along the subterranean tunnels of...",sec={{t="Gems of the Deep",b="Discovered within the watery cavern entrances of Blackfathom Deeps along Ashenvale's Zoram Strand, Sapphires of Aku'Mai are crystalline formations rich in elemental energy. The spirits of water cling tightly to them, making them exceptional catalysts for magical workings. When scouts reported that the subterranean naga had begun actively quarrying these clusters from the cavern walls, the Shaman Je'neu Sancrea sought adventuring assistance to confiscate them. Left in the serpent peoples' clutches, the stones could easily fuel devastating arcane rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Sapphire of Aku'Mai?",a="They are vibrant sapphire crystals found lining the walls of Blackfathom Deeps. Bound closely with the elemental spirits of water, they hold deep arcane and elemental resonance.",al={"what is this crystal","sapphire of aku'mai lore","what are these gems"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the naga collecting these sapphires?",a="Their exact intentions remain uncertain, but Je'neu Sancrea suspects the naga intended to harness the crystals' rich water and arcane energies for dangerous sorcery within the submerged temple.",al={"why do naga want sapphires","naga crystal harvesting"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is looking for these sapphires?",a="Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, tasks travelers with gathering them to keep them out of naga hands.",al={"who wants sapphires of akumai","who turns in essence of akumai"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are these crystals directly tied to the beast Aku'mai?",a="While named after Aku'mai, the monstrous hydra inhabiting the deeps, the crystals grow naturally in the cavern walls. Their naming reflects their proximity to the dark presence lurking within the ruins.",al={"aku'mai connection","is it from akumai"},it="ties"},{q="Where do the Sapphires of Aku'Mai come from, and who made them?",a="These large sapphire clusters grow naturally along the cavern walls within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps. They are not crafted by mortal hands; rather, they are natural mineral formations steeped in the cavern's ambient energies. Water spirits naturally cling to the crystals, granting them inherent elemental potency.",al={"origin of sapphire of aku'mai","who made sapphire of akumai","where do sapphires of aku'mai come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Earthen Ring shamans like Je'neu Sancrea readily perceive the water spirits bound within these gems, treating the naga harvest as an elemental threat.",["class:Mage"]="The innate water saturation makes these raw sapphires highly valued as conduits for potent arcane components."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","crystals","je'neu sancrea","naga","sapphire","water spirits","zoram strand"},rel={"quest:6563","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:naga","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:6562","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Sapphire of Aku'Mai","The Essence of Aku'Mai (Classic)"}}
E["item:twilight-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Twilight Pendant",z="blackfathom",s="A Twilight Pendant is an insignia worn by cultists of the Twilight's Hammer deep within Blackfathom Deeps. To the Argent Dawn, these dark talismans serve as definitive proof of the cult's subversive operations on the coast of Ashenvale.",h="A Twilight Pendant is an insignia worn by cultists of the Twilight's Hammer deep within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Tokens of the Old Gods",b="Within the drowned ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, members of the Twilight's Hammer gather alongside the naga to conduct foul rites in veneration of the chaotic Old Gods. Cultists—ranging from shadowmages and aquamancers to reavers and loreseekers—wear these pendants as emblems of devotion to their shadowy patrons. Because the cult operates in secrecy beneath the former night elf temple, retrieving these ornaments is one of the few ways outside observers can gauge the cult's numbers and thwart their machinations.",sp=0},{t="The Argent Dawn's Vigils",b="Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus actively seeks these pendants as evidence of a successful purge against the encroaching darkness. Blackfathom Deeps once housed a pristine moonwell, and its desecration by malevolent void-worshipers poses a severe threat to Kalimdor. Gathering the pendants confirms that the cultists' foothold in Ashenvale is being dismantled before their dark patrons can unleash greater terror.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Twilight Pendant?",a="A Twilight Pendant is an identifying amulet worn by members of the Twilight's Hammer cult operating within Blackfathom Deeps. It serves as tangible proof of devotion to the Old Gods and their dark rites.",al={"twilight pendant info","what are twilight pendants"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Manados want these pendants?",a="Argent Guard Manados, stationed in Darnassus on behalf of the Argent Dawn, seeks them as proof that the Twilight's Hammer presence in Blackfathom Deeps is being struck down before their evil plans can mature.",al={"who wants twilight pendant","why collect twilight pendants"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wears these pendants?",a="They are carried by various cultists inside the submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps, including Twilight Acolytes, Aquamancers, Shadowmages, Loreseekers, Elementalists, and Reavers.",al={"who drops twilight pendant","where do twilight pendants come from"},it="people"},{q="What threat does the Twilight's Hammer pose in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Allied with the naga, the Twilight's Hammer aims to revive the worship of the Old Gods, desecrating an ancient night elf moonwell and preparing rituals that could spread terror across Kalimdor.",al={"what is twilights hammer doing in bfd","why are cultists in ashenvale"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of Blackfathom Deeps—once home to a revered and powerful moonwell—makes reclaiming these symbols of corruption a matter of profound sanctity for the kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="Carried to Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus, these trophies demonstrate that the Alliance is actively supporting the Argent Dawn's crusade against hidden evils in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"argent guard manados","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","old gods","twilight falls","twilight pendant","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:1199","npc:argent-guard-manados","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus"},src={"Twilight Pendant","Twilight Falls (Classic)"}}
E["npc:aku-mai"] = {t="npc",n="Aku'mai",z="blackfathom",s="Aku'mai is a monstrous, three-headed hydra dwelling in the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand. Imbued with primordial shadow and favored by the ancient Old Gods, the beast is revered as a herald of apocalyptic ruin. The Twilight's Hammer cult tends to the creature in its submerged lair, offering living sacrifices to sate its eternal hunger.",h="Aku'mai is a monstrous, three-headed hydra dwelling in the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram...",sec={{t="The Scourge of Zoram Strand",b="Long before cultists claimed the sunken temple beneath the sea, Aku'mai haunted the coast of Ashenvale as a living blight upon the Zoram Strand. A creature of deep water and darker powers, this gargantuan hydra carries a fragment of the Old Gods' ancient malevolence within its three ravenous heads. Rather than an ordinary denizen of the tides, Aku'mai is an ancient terror that has lurked in the submerged ruins since the fall of the night elves' temple to Elune, poisoning the waters with Void-tainted malice.",sp=0},{t="A Pet of the Primordial Darkness",b="Aku'mai's foul aura eventually drew the Twilight's Hammer deep into the subterranean caverns. Viewing the hydra as an anointed pet and harbinger of their dread masters, the cult established their sanctum around its nesting ground. Twilight Lord Kelris became consumed by the creature, convinced that tending to Aku'mai and facilitating its unending appetite would usher in the resurgence of the Old Gods and grant him eternal life. Cultists and captured captives alike are regularly cast into the hydra's pool to nourish its vile growth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is an ancient, three-headed hydra infused with dark Void energies. Originating as a favored pet of the Old Gods, it has haunted the Zoram Strand and the submerged halls of Blackfathom Deeps for generations.",al={"who is akumai","akumai lore","what kind of monster is akumai"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Aku'mai live?",a="Aku'mai resides in the deepest submerged grottos of Blackfathom Deeps, a ruined temple complex dedicated to Elune located along the coast of the Zoram Strand in north-western Ashenvale.",al={"akumai location","where is akumai","where can i find akumai"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer feeding Aku'mai?",a="The Twilight's Hammer views Aku'mai as an emissary and herald of their Old God masters. Led by Twilight Lord Kelris, the cultists offer living sacrifices to feed the beast's hunger, believing that nourishing it will hasten the return of the Old Gods and reward them with dark blessings.",al={"why are cultists feeding akumai","kelris akumai","twilights hammer akumai"},it="motive"},{q="What powers does Aku'mai possess?",a="Beyond its immense physical size and multiple snapping heads, Aku'mai channels shadow and Void energy gifted by the Old Gods. Its presence corrupts surrounding waters and instills madness in those who draw near.",al={"akumai powers","is akumai magical","void hydra"},it="power"},{q="Is Aku'mai an Old God?",a="No. Aku'mai is not an Old God, but rather a primordial hydra serving as their favored pet and conduit. It holds a tiny fraction of their ancient dark power, sufficient to drive cultists to worship it.",al={"is akumai an old god","is akumai a god"},it="origin"},{q="Why do adventurers venture into the deeps to slay it?",a="Left unchecked, Aku'mai's endless hunger and the cult's sacrifices threaten to unleash a calamitous evil across Ashenvale and Kalimdor. Both Alliance and Horde authorities seek to put an end to the Twilight's Hammer and slay the horror lurking at the heart of the temple.",al={"why kill akumai","blackfathom villainy akumai","akumai threat"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Aku'mai on?",a="Aku'mai serves the primordial Old Gods as their ancient, favored pet. The hydra holds no allegiance to mortal races, though the Twilight's Hammer cult actively tends to the beast, feeding it living sacrifices in desperate hopes of winning the favor of its dark masters.",al={"akumai faction","who does akumai serve","akumai loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Aku'mai want?",a="Imbued with Void energy and a sliver of the Old Gods' dread power, Aku'mai is driven by a ravenous and monstrous hunger. The beast seeks only to slaughter, feed, and ultimately devour the world, spurred on by the cultists offering fresh meat to fuel its growth.",al={"akumai goal","what does akumai desire","akumai purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Aku'mai here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Aku'mai took up residence within the sunken temple ruins beneath the Zoram Strand ages ago, ravaging the shoreline as an ancient scourge. The sunken sanctuaries of Blackfathom Deeps provide a dark, watery haven where the Twilight's Hammer cult can easily shelter, feed, and worship it in secret.",al={"why is akumai in blackfathom","how did akumai get here","akumai zhang strand"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Aku'mai tied to?",a="Aku'mai is tied directly to the Old Gods as their monstrous creation and favored pet. In Blackfathom Deeps, it is tended by Twilight Lord Kelris, who considers the beast a herald of the Old Gods' return and nurtures its growth with endless cultist and captive sacrifices.",al={"akumai connections","who controls akumai","akumai and kelris"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Aku'mai so feared?",a="Aku'mai has terrorized the Zoram Strand for ages as a gargantuan, three-headed terror steeped in Void energies. Tales of its insatiable hunger and the horrifying worship it commands from the Twilight's Hammer make it one of the most dreaded primeval evils lurking along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"why is akumai feared","akumai reputation","is akumai dangerous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Aku'mai has defiled the deepest sanctorum of a ruined temple once consecrated to the moon-goddess Elune, turning a holy site into a pit of sacrifice.",["class:Priest"]="The vile presence of Aku'mai and the Twilight's Hammer represents the direct corruption of the Void against the teachings of the Holy Light and Elune.",["class:Druid"]="Aku'mai's unnatural corruption warps the coastal waters of Ashenvale, demanding cleansing to restore natural balance."},kw={"aku'mai","akumai","blackfathom","deeps","hydra","kelris","old god","zoram"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:1200","topic:elune"},src={"Aku'mai"}}
E["npc:argent-guard-manados"] = {t="npc",n="Argent Guard Manados",z="blackfathom",s="Argent Guard Manados is a night elf sentry stationed in Darnassus on behalf of the Argent Dawn. Resting at the Craftsmen's Terrace, he keeps watch over Kalimdor's growing corruption and directs adventurers toward the sinister forces lurking in Blackfathom Deeps.",h="Argent Guard Manados is a night elf sentry stationed in Darnassus on behalf of the Argent Dawn.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of the Dawn",b="While most of the Argent Dawn focuses its vigilance on the blighted lands of Lordaeron and the Scourge, Argent Guard Manados represents their watchful eyes in the night elf capital of Darnassus. Standing among the artisans and tradefolk of the Craftsmen's Terrace, Manados monitors emerging threats that menace the balance of northern Kalimdor. When rumors reach him of the Twilight's Hammer cult establishing a foul foothold beneath the waves of Ashenvale, Manados enlists capable heroes to strike at Blackfathom Deeps and recover artifacts of their dark devotion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Manados?",a="Manados is a night elf operative of the Argent Dawn stationed in Darnassus. Rather than battling the Scourge in the Eastern Kingdoms, he remains in Kalimdor to keep watch for dark cults and otherworldly corruption.",al={"who is manados","argent guard manados role","manados darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Argent Guard Manados?",a="He can be found standing in the Craftsmen's Terrace within Darnassus, watching over the city and coordinating with local adventurers.",al={"manados location","where is argent guard manados","manados craftsman terrace"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Argent Guard Manados give?",a="He offers the quest 'Twilight Falls', tasking adventurers to enter Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale and retrieve Twilight Pendants from the cultists lurking inside.",al={"manados quests","twilight falls quest giver","blackfathom deeps argent dawn quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Argent Dawn combats malignant forces that threaten Azeroth. The sudden emergence of the Twilight's Hammer cult worshipping ancient, corrupt entities in the submerged ruins of Ashenvale presents a peril they cannot ignore.",al={"why argent dawn bfd","argent dawn twilight cult"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Argent Guard Manados on?",a="Argent Guard Manados serves the Argent Dawn, an independent order dedicated to eradicating evil and protecting Azeroth from dark corruption. Though he is a night elf stationed within the capital city of Darnassus, his primary allegiance lies with the Dawn's global crusade rather than standard Alliance command.",al={"manados faction","who does manados serve","is manados alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Argent Guard Manados want?",a="Manados seeks to stop the dark rituals taking root along the Ashenvale coast. He enlists capable adventurers to delve into Blackfathom Deeps and strike against the Twilight's Hammer cultists who have desecrated the ancient night elven sanctuary.",al={"what is manados looking for","manados goals","why send to blackfathom"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Manados shows that not all night elves limit their duty to the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels; some dedicate their lives to neutral cross-faction orders like the Argent Dawn to preserve Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions visiting Darnassus, Manados provides a crucial link between the distant crusades in Lordaeron and the creeping menace of cultists in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"argent dawn","argent guard manados","blackfathom deeps","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","manados","twilight falls"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","zone:blackfathom","quest:1199","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","topic:night-elf"},src={"Argent Guard Manados"}}
E["npc:baron-aquanis"] = {t="npc",n="Baron Aquanis",z="blackfathom",s="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental of the flooded Moonshrine Ruins in Blackfathom Deeps, where the Twilight's Hammer has made its lair. He rises from the deep water when someone disturbs the ruins' Fathom Stone. The shamans of the Earthen Ring have long thought him a corrupted elemental power, and they suspect the cult is behind it.",h="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental of the flooded Moonshrine Ruins in Blackfathom Deeps, where the...",sec={{t="Guardian of the Fathom Stone",b="Submerged beneath the flooded halls of the Moonshrine Ruins, the Fathom Stone lies right under the noses of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who now occupy the ruins. Inside it is a fathom core, a device that, properly read, tells the history of all elemental activity around it. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring sends Horde adventurers to recover the core, and disturbing the stone draws Baron Aquanis up from the depths.",sp=0},{t="Corruption of the Depths",b="The Earthen Ring has long thought of Baron Aquanis as a corrupted elemental power. When he is destroyed, he leaves behind a Strange Water Globe: an impervious orb of putrid, sloshing water that seems to have fed him energy. Je'neu Sancrea believes the globe will prove what corrupted the baron, and how. It would be no surprise to him if it turned out to be the Twilight's Hammer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis dwells in the flooded Moonshrine Ruins deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. He doesn't roam the halls: he rises from the water when the ruins' underwater Fathom Stone is disturbed, which Horde adventurers do while recovering its fathom core for Je'neu Sancrea.",al={"aquanis location","where is baron aquanis","how to spawn baron aquanis"}},{q="What is the Strange Water Globe?",a="The Strange Water Globe is what Baron Aquanis leaves behind when he is destroyed: an orb that no physical force can break, with putrid water sloshing inside. It seems to have fed the elemental energy. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring wants to study it, believing it will prove what corrupted the baron and how it was done.",al={"strange water globe","aquanis globe","what is the water globe for"}},{q="Why is the Earthen Ring interested in Baron Aquanis?",a="The Earthen Ring watches over the balance of the elements. Je'neu Sancrea and his comrades have long thought Baron Aquanis a corrupted elemental power, and with the Twilight's Hammer now in the Moonshrine Ruins they fear the cult is coercing the elements to work against the Horde. The baron's remains and the ruins' fathom core could show them what the cult is up to.",al={"why earthen ring care","je'neu sancrea aquanis"}},{q="What is the Fathom Core?",a="The Fathom Core is an elemental artifact housed within the sunken Fathom Stone. When properly read by a trained shaman, it reveals a comprehensive history of regional elemental activity, exposing whatever dark rituals the Twilight's Hammer are conducting in the ruins.",al={"fathom core lore","what does fathom core do"}},{q="Is Baron Aquanis allied with the Twilight's Hammer?",a="Not by choice, as far as anyone can tell. The Earthen Ring considers him a corrupted elemental rather than a willing servant, and the Twilight's Hammer cultists who hold the Moonshrine Ruins are the obvious suspects. Je'neu Sancrea says it would be no surprise if they were behind it, but he wants proof before he says for sure.",al={"is aquanis twilight hammer","aquanis cult"}},{q="Does the Alliance have business with Baron Aquanis?",a="Not directly. The Fathom Stone, and with it Baron Aquanis, are Je'neu Sancrea's concern: he is an Earthen Ring shaman working with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast, and it is Horde adventurers he sends to recover the fathom core. Alliance explorers in Blackfathom Deeps have other errands there.",al={"can alliance fight aquanis","alliance aquanis quest"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For shamans of the Earthen Ring, Baron Aquanis is a tragic example of elemental perversion, whose tainted remains offer crucial insights into purifying twisted spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu Sancrea works with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast, and the fathom core his Horde helpers recover is meant to show what the Twilight's Hammer is doing to the elements there."},kw={"aquanis","baron aquanis","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","water elemental"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:6921","quest:6922","item:fathom-core","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:horde"},src={"Baron Aquanis","Baron Aquanis (quest)","Amongst the Ruins"}}
E["npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm"] = {t="npc",n="Dawnwatcher Selgorm",z="blackfathom",s="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is a human representative of the Argent Dawn stationed upon the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. Acting as an observer and liaison in the night elven capital, he monitors reports of shadowy cult activity and dark threats stirring across northern Kalimdor.",h="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is a human representative of the Argent Dawn stationed upon the Craftsmen's Terrace in...",sec={{t="Eyes in the World Tree",b="While the Argent Dawn focuses heavily on the undead scourge festering in the Eastern Plaguelands, their vigilance extends anywhere ancient evil takes root. Dawnwatcher Selgorm stands watch in Darnassus, bridging the gap between the insular night elves and the broader crusade against malevolence. From the Craftsmen's Terrace, he gathers intelligence on emerging threats in Kalimdor's wilderness, enlisting capable Alliance travelers to strike at cultists and dark powers before their influence can corrupt the realm.",sp=0},{t="A Strike Against Darkness",b="Selgorm's primary concern is Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. Recognizing the vile convergence of the Twilight's Hammer cult and serpentine naga beneath the waves, he rewards the seasoned champions who venture into the flooded ruins. By targeting the cult's wicked leaders and reclaiming tainted relics, he hopes to quell the growing shadows threatening Kalimdor's sacred shores.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm?",a="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is a human agent of the Argent Dawn. He is stationed in the night elven capital of Darnassus to watch for encroaching evil across Kalimdor.",al={"selgorm","who is selgorm","dawnwatcher selgorm lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Dawnwatcher Selgorm be found?",a="He can be found standing outdoors upon the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, overlooking the bustling workshops of the night elven capital.",al={"selgorm location","where is selgorm","selgorm darnassus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member stationed in Darnassus?",a="While the Argent Dawn is famous for fighting the Scourge in Lordaeron, the order is dedicated to rooting out malevolence everywhere. Selgorm monitors rising cult activity, such as the Twilight's Hammer, in northern Kalimdor.",al={"argent dawn in darnassus","why is argent dawn here"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Selgorm ask adventurers to do?",a="Selgorm awaits Alliance heroes returning from Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale with the head of Twilight Lord Kelris, the Twilight's Hammer leader there, whom the wounded Argent Guard Thaelrid urges them to slay to stop the cult's corruption from spreading.",al={"selgorm quest","blackfathom villainy quest giver"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Dawnwatcher Selgorm on?",a="Selgorm is an agent of the Argent Dawn, a neutral order dedicated to safeguarding Azeroth from corruption and darkness. While the Dawn operates independently of factional politics, Selgorm makes his camp among the night elves in Darnassus to solicit help from Alliance champions willing to strike at vile cults.",al={"selgorm faction","who does selgorm serve","is selgorm alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm tied to?",a="Selgorm answers directly to the Argent Dawn. Though stationed in the night elf capital of Darnassus, his duty is tied to his order's global vigil rather than the Kaldorei leadership, monitoring shadowy threats that fester far from the order's primary strongholds in the Plaguelands.",al={"selgorm argent dawn","who does selgorm work with","selgorm allies"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers exploring northern Kalimdor, Selgorm serves as a vital bridge between Darnassus and the crusade against sinister cults hiding along the coast.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers visiting the remote boughs of Teldrassil may find comfort in encountering a fellow countryman working in service to the noble Argent Dawn."},kw={"argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","dawnwatcher selgorm","twilight's hammer"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","topic:alliance","quest:940"},src={"Dawnwatcher Selgorm"}}
E["npc:dawnwatcher-shaedlass"] = {t="npc",n="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass",z="blackfathom",s="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is a night elf affiliated with the Argent Dawn, stationed within the Craftsmen's Terrace of Darnassus. Acting as a quiet eyes-and-ears operative in Kalimdor, he seeks news of his fellow order members sent on perilous reconnaissance into hostile lands.",h="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is a night elf affiliated with the Argent Dawn, stationed within the Craftsmen's...",sec={{t="Eyes of the Argent Dawn",b="While the Argent Dawn is most famous for its bitter crusade against the Scourge in the Eastern Plaguelands, its vigilance extends far beyond Lordaeron. Dawnwatcher Shaedlass maintains a presence in the night elven capital of Darnassus, watching over the faction's interests in Kalimdor. From his quiet post on the Craftsmen's Terrace, he keeps tabs on covert expeditions against dark cults and corrupting powers that threaten the wider world.",sp=0},{t="A Missing Brother",b="Shaedlass's chief concern is the whereabouts of Argent Guard Thaelrid, a comrade dispatched south to investigate reports of insidious cult activity within the Blackfathom Deeps along the Ashenvale coast. Fearing Thaelrid has met with foul play among the Twilight's Hammer and the aquatic horrors of the ancient elven temple, Shaedlass actively enlists daring Alliance adventurers to infiltrate the ruins and discover the scout's fate.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is a night elf agent of the Argent Dawn. He is posted on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, serving as a liaison and point of contact for the order's efforts in northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is shaedlass","dawnwatcher shaedlass lore","argent dawn darnassus npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member in Darnassus?",a="Although the Argent Dawn primarily wages war against the Scourge in Lordaeron, they maintain vigilant agents across Azeroth to track corrupting evils. Shaedlass coordinates intelligence and monitors threats brewing across Kalimdor, including shadowy cults.",al={"why is argent dawn in darnassus","argent dawn night elf"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Shaedlass ask adventurers to do?",a="Shaedlass sends Alliance adventurers into the sunken temple of Blackfathom Deeps on the quest 'In Search of Thaelrid'. He tasks them with finding Argent Guard Thaelrid, an undercover scout who ventured into the ruins to investigate the Twilight's Hammer and never reported back.",al={"shaedlass quest","in search of thaelrid quest"},it="wants"},{q="Where can I find Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="He is located in Darnassus on the Craftsmen's Terrace, situated near the trade vendors and craftsmen of the capital.",al={"shaedlass location","where is dawnwatcher shaedlass"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass on?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass serves the Argent Dawn, a neutral coalition dedicated to fighting evil wherever it threatens Azeroth. Though he is a night elf residing in the capital city of Darnassus, his primary allegiance lies with the Dawn rather than strictly the Alliance, allowing him to focus on broader perils like cultists and the Scourge.",al={"shaedlass faction","who does shaedlass serve","is shaedlass alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass tied to?",a="Shaedlass answers directly to the Argent Dawn. He is particularly concerned with the fate of his fellow agent, Argent Guard Thaelrid, who was sent to investigate the foul corruption taking root within Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale.",al={"shaedlass connections","who does shaedlass work with","shaedlass argent dawn ties"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Shaedlass provides Alliance heroes in Darnassus a direct link to the mysteries of Blackfathom Deeps, dispatching scouts to rescue an operative deep behind enemy lines.",["race:NightElf"]="As one of the few night elves openly serving under the banner of the Argent Dawn, Shaedlass bridges the insular politics of Teldrassil with a global vigil against darkness."},kw={"argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","dawnwatcher","shaedlass","thaelrid"},rel={"quest:1198","zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","topic:argent-dawn","zone:blackfathom","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Dawnwatcher Shaedlass"}}
E["npc:gelihast"] = {t="npc",n="Gelihast",z="blackfathom",s="Gelihast is a ferocious, twin-blade wielding murloc chieftain residing in the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Lured by the dark whispers of the Old Gods, he butchered his way into the sunken temple ruins before earning the reluctant respect of the Twilight's Hammer cultists.",h="Gelihast is a ferocious, twin-blade wielding murloc chieftain residing in the Pool of Ask'ar within...",sec={{t="A Deadly Calling",b="While most murlocs stay near coastal shallows, Gelihast felt the dark, ominous tug of the Old Gods deep beneath Ashenvale. Driven by these primordial whispers, he forced his way into the sunken temple of Blackfathom Deeps. When Twilight's Hammer cultists tried to halt his path, he slaughtered nearly a dozen of them single-handedly using his twin swords.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Blindlight",b="Rather than seeking vengeance, the cultists admired Gelihast's raw savagery and granted him dominion over the Pool of Ask'ar. There, surrounded by his Blindlight brood, the bloodthirsty murloc constructed a crude altar. He performs grim sacrifices upon it, receiving dark boons directly from the foul presence slumbering in the abyss.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gelihast?",a="Gelihast is a vicious murloc chieftain who commands the Blindlight tribe inside the Pool of Ask'ar in Blackfathom Deeps. He fights with twin blades and serves the dark presence lingering within the ruins.",al={"who is gelihast","gelihast lore","gelihast background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gelihast inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="He was drawn by the whispers of the Old Gods. Desiring to reach the source of the dark call, he invaded the ruins and carved a bloody path through the local cultists to claim his own territory.",al={"why is there a murloc in bfd","why is gelihast in the temple"},it="why_here"},{q="How did the Twilight's Hammer react to him?",a="Although Gelihast slaughtered nearly a dozen Twilight's Hammer cultists upon entering the temple, the survivors were so impressed by his ferocity and cruelty that they permitted him to stay and worship alongside them.",al={"gelihast and twilights hammer","do cultists like gelihast"},it="side"},{q="What is the altar behind Gelihast?",a="Gelihast erected the shrine to offer bloody sacrifices to the ominous presence in the ruins. Travelers who defeat him can touch the altar to receive the Blessing of Blackfathom.",al={"altar of the deep","gelihast altar","blessing of blackfathom altar"}},{q="What tribe of murlocs does he lead?",a="He leads the Blindlight murlocs, an aggressive tribe that infests the Pool of Ask'ar within the caverns.",al={"gelihast tribe","what murlocs are in bfd"},it="ties"},{q="What happens to Gelihast if he is left unchecked?",a="He continues to sacrifice victims at his altar in the Pool of Ask'ar, serving as a vicious enforcer and fanatic servant of the shadowy horrors infesting the ruins.",al={"gelihast fate","who kills gelihast"}},{q="What does Gelihast want?",a="Gelihast seeks to honor and serve the Old Gods whose dark whispers drew him into the sunken temple. Having claimed a corner of the ruins through sheer bloodshed, he desires nothing more than to offer blood sacrifices at his personal shrine and bask in the dark blessings granted by the ancient horrors lurking deep beneath the waters.",al={"gelihast goal","what does gelihast want","gelihast motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Gelihast attacks with blinding sword speed; skilled warriors who brace themselves can turn his frantic dual-wielding assault entirely against him.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces seeking to cleanse the corruption leaking into Ashenvale, removing Gelihast is essential to secure the northern passages of the submerged temple.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers dispatched to scour Blackfathom Deeps must eliminate Gelihast to disrupt the cultist alliance festering beneath the Zoram Strand."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","blindlight","gelihast","murloc","old gods","pool of ask'ar","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:murloc","npc:lady-sarevess"},src={"Gelihast"}}
E["npc:gershala-nightwhisper"] = {t="npc",n="Gershala Nightwhisper",z="blackfathom",s="Gershala Nightwhisper is a night elf researcher residing in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore. Driven by grave concern over the path taken by the high elves of Quel'Thalas, he studies specimens of cursed aquatic and demonic creatures to understand how magical corruption warps both mind and body.",h="Gershala Nightwhisper is a night elf researcher residing in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore.",sec={{t="Study of Transformation",b="Stationed peacefully within Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper looks beyond the immediate coastal troubles of Darkshore toward a broader, creeping danger. Watching with dismay as the remaining high elves embrace perilous arcane practices and dub themselves blood elves, Gershala seeks to understand the biological and spiritual descent that follows unchecked magic. To unlock these secrets, he directs seasoned Alliance adventurers into the submerged halls of Blackfathom Deeps to harvest corrupted brain stems from the naga and satyr who dwell within.",sp=0},{t="An Antidote to Ruin",b="Gershala's grim focus on brain stems from naga and satyr stems from their shared lineage: both races were once night elves before yielding to Queen Azshara and demonic bargains. By dissecting the physical marks left upon their nervous systems by millennia of demonic and abyssal energies, he hopes to uncover warnings or safeguards that might keep other elven kin from plunging into similar monstrous deformity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Gershala Nightwhisper found?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper can be found in Auberdine, the main Alliance port town located on the coast of Darkshore.",al={"gershala location","where is gershala","find gershala nightwhisper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gershala want naga and satyr brain stems?",a="Gershala studies corrupted brain stems to examine how profound magical and demonic transformation alters the anatomy of former night elves. Both naga and satyr were once elves, and he aims to understand the physical mechanisms behind their corruption.",al={"why brain stems","researching the corruption lore","what does gershala study"},it="wants"},{q="What does Gershala hope to accomplish with his research?",a="Gershala hopes his research will provide crucial insights to prevent the blood elves from devolving into evil and monstrous deformity through their dangerous reliance on fel and unchecked arcane power.",al={"gershala goal","why help blood elves","gershala research purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the specimens Gershala needs located?",a="He directs adventurers to Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient submerged temple ruin on the coast of Ashenvale infested with both naga and satyr.",al={"where are the stems","blackfathom deeps stems","where to find gershala items"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Gershala Nightwhisper?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper is a night elf scholar residing in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore. Driven by scholarly curiosity and concern for the wider world, he dedicates himself to understanding magical and biological corruption. He studies the altered anatomy of creatures warped by dark powers, hoping that careful study can prevent similar downfalls among other peoples.",al={"who is gershala","gershala nightwhisper lore","gershala background"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Gershala Nightwhisper on?",a="Gershala is allied with the night elves of Darnassus and serves as a friendly scholar to members of the Alliance. His research takes place in Auberdine, where he works to protect Kalimdor and the broader mortal races from the creeping threats of demonic and magical degradation.",al={"gershala faction","is gershala alliance","gershala allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Gershala Nightwhisper here?",a="Gershala makes his home in Auberdine because Darkshore lies directly adjacent to places deeply infested by ancient evils, such as Blackfathom Deeps. From this coastal haven, he can recruit travelers and adventurers venturing south to gather corrupted specimens for his ongoing research.",al={"why is gershala in auberdine","gershala purpose darkshore"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Gershala's grim inquiries are a poignant reminder of the ancient Sundering and the terrible cost of magical addiction, which once reshaped their brethren into horrors.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gershala serves as a primary patron sending Alliance expeditions toward the hazards of Blackfathom Deeps, ensuring their incursions yield valuable arcane knowledge."},kw={"auberdine","blackfathom","corruption","darkshore","gershala","naga","nightwhisper","satyr"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1275","zone:blackfathom","topic:night-elf","topic:satyr","topic:naga","quest:3765"},src={"Gershala Nightwhisper"}}
E["npc:ghamoo-ra-classic"] = {t="npc",n="Ghamoo-ra",z="blackfathom",s="Ghamoo-ra is an ancient, giant sea turtle inhabiting the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Once a peaceful denizen of Elune's sunken temple, he was captured, tortured, and driven mad by the Twilight's Hammer cult to serve as a vicious guardian.",h="Ghamoo-ra is an ancient, giant sea turtle inhabiting the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Gentle Beast Tormented",b="Before the defilement of Blackfathom Deeps, Ghamoo-ra was among the last peaceful natural inhabitants dwelling among the flooded ruins of the night elven temple dedicated to Elune. When the nihilistic Twilight's Hammer cult took control of the sanctuary, they roused the ancient turtle from his quiet life and locked him in captivity. Rather than slain, he was systematically tormented for years, suffering mental and physical flaying at the hands of the cultists.",sp=0},{t="Guardian of the Deeps",b="Broken by prolonged cruelty, the great turtle finally succumbed to madness. Bestowing the name Ghamoo-ra upon the ruined creature, the cultists trained him into a ferocious defense beast. Now patrolling a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar surrounded by lesser turtles, Ghamoo-ra blindly attacks any intruders who enter the caverns, serving the very cult that shattered his mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ghamoo-ra?",a="Ghamoo-ra is a giant turtle found in the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps. Originally a peaceful dweller of the temple of Elune, he was captured, tortured, and broken into a ferocious guard beast by the Twilight's Hammer cult.",al={"ghamoo-ra lore","giant turtle bfd","who is ghamoo ra"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ghamoo-ra hostile to outsiders?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult imprisoned the turtle and tortured him over several years, breaking his spirit and driving him to utter madness. They conditioned him to lash out at any outsider who approaches the inner shrines.",al={"why is turtle angry","why does turtle attack","ghamoo-ra madness"},it="hostile"},{q="Can a hunter tame Ghamoo-ra?",a="Yes. Despite his size and years of torment, Ghamoo-ra can be tamed by a skilled hunter.",al={"tame ghamoo-ra","can hunter tame bfd turtle"},gp=true},{q="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?",a="The Pool of Ask'ar is a flooded subterranean cavern in Blackfathom Deeps. Ghamoo-ra roams the center of a small island there, encircled by docile native turtles.",al={"pool of ask'ar","where is ghamoo ra"},it="place"},{q="What connection does he have to the Old Gods?",a="While not inherently a creature of the Void, Ghamoo-ra's mind was warped by Twilight's Hammer cultists who worship the Old Gods. They twisted the ancient creature into an unwitting protector of their dark ritual grounds.",al={"ghamoo-ra old gods","is turtle corrupted"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Ghamoo-ra on?",a="Ghamoo-ra serves the Twilight's Hammer cultists who occupy Blackfathom Deeps, though not by choice. Once a gentle dweller of the temple, he was broken and conditioned through years of relentless cruelty to guard the shrine of the Old Gods and eliminate any trespassers who venture near.",al={"ghamoora faction","who does ghamoo-ra serve","is ghamoo-ra twilight hammer"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Ghamoo-ra want?",a="Ghamoo-ra has no grand ambitions of his own. Driven completely mad by the dark rituals and torment inflicted by the Twilight's Hammer, the giant turtle is consumed by pain and confusion, lashing out blindly to crush intruders and defend the cavern where he is held captive.",al={"ghamoora goal","what does the turtle want","ghamoora motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Ghamoo-ra here?",a="Ghamoo-ra originally inhabited the sunken temple when it was a peaceful sanctuary dedicated to the moon goddess Elune. When the Twilight's Hammer moved into Blackfathom Deeps, they captured and chained him within the Pool of Ask'ar, turning him into a monstrous, living weapon to guard their path.",al={"why is ghamoo-ra in blackfathom deeps","ghamoo-ra pool of ask'ar why","why is there a giant turtle here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Hunters venturing into Blackfathom Deeps may pity Ghamoo-ra, a noble, ancient beast broken by dark captivity, though a patient hunter may yet tame him.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ghamoo-ra's plight is a bitter reminder of the defilement of Elune's sacred temple by the vile Twilight's Hammer.",["class:Druid"]="Druids view Ghamoo-ra's torment and forced aggression as a tragic corruption of natural wildlife by the servants of the Old Gods."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","elune","ghamoo-ra","pool of ask'ar","tame","turtle","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:elune","topic:old-god"},src={"Ghamoo-ra (Classic)"}}
E["npc:je-neu-sancrea"] = {t="npc",n="Je'neu Sancrea",z="blackfathom",s="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll and a member of the Earthen Ring stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the Ashenvale coast. Sensing dark disturbances deep beneath the shoreline, he directs Horde adventurers to investigate the corruption infesting the ancient submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps.",h="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll and a member of the Earthen Ring stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the...",sec={{t="A Shaman on the Strand",b="While most of the Earthen Ring focuses on elemental harmony across Kalimdor, Je'neu Sancrea keeps watch over the secluded and dangerous Zoram Strand. Perched at Zoram'gar Outpost, he observes the dark tremors and unnatural tides stirring near the ruined temple of Blackfathom Deeps. Though bound by the shamanic duties of his circle, his strong loyalties to the Darkspear tribe and Thrall's Horde keep him working exclusively alongside Horde champions.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Deep",b="Je'neu seeks to uncover the true cause behind the creeping corruption around the coast. Through bold adventurers, he collects tainted sapphire cores, investigates the vile remnants of water elementals like Baron Aquanis, and uncovers the insidious influence of the Twilight's Hammer cult. The dark rituals taking place beneath the waves threaten not only the balance of the local elements, but herald the dark return of forces sworn to the Old Gods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll shaman affiliated with the Earthen Ring. He is stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Ashenvale coast, where he monitors the growing corruption spilling out from Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who is jeneu","jeneu sancrea lore","what is jeneu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Je'neu only deal with Horde adventurers if he is Earthen Ring?",a="Although the Earthen Ring as an organization pursues elemental balance rather than faction warfare, Je'neu's personal ties remain firmly rooted in the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Because he resides within a frontline Horde military outpost in Ashenvale, he does not welcome Alliance travelers.",al={"why horde only","can alliance talk to jeneu","is jeneu neutral"},it="side"},{q="What is Je'neu investigating in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Je'neu investigates the unnatural elemental unrest and dark magic rising from Blackfathom Deeps. He charges champions with retrieving corrupted water cores, slaying Twilight's Hammer cultists, and confirming whispers that an ancient hydra, Aku'mai, serves ancient malevolent masters beneath the sea.",al={"jeneu quest goals","what does jeneu want","why send players to bfd"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu is located at Zoram'gar Outpost, a fortified Horde settlement on the far northwestern coast of Ashenvale, right along the Zoram Strand just south of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is jeneu","jeneu sancrea location","find jeneu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an ancient circle of shamans dedicated to understanding and soothing the elemental spirits of the world, intervening whenever dark forces or chaotic entities disrupt natural elemental harmony.",al={"earthen ring lore","what is the earthen ring","shaman organization"},it="ties"},{q="What is the threat of the Twilight's Hammer in the Deeps?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult has infiltrated Blackfathom Deeps to venerate the beast Aku'mai and conduct rituals dedicated to the Old Gods. Je'neu tasks Horde adventurers with cutting down their leaders to halt their dark work.",al={"twilights hammer bfd","twilight cult ashenvale","who are the cultists in bfd"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Je'neu Sancrea here?",a="Je'neu has stationed himself at the Zoram'gar Outpost along the Ashenvale coast to observe the sinister corruption stirring in the nearby ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. The Earthen Ring sensed foul disturbances in the natural balance of the waters, drawing him to this frontier to monitor the gathering cultists and enlist seasoned Horde champions to scour the depths.",al={"why is jeneu in ashenvale","why is jeneu sancrea at zoramgar","what brings jeneu sancrea here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a prominent Darkspear member of the Earthen Ring, Je'neu represents the shamanic duty to balance corrupted elementals and restore balance to the waters of Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu serves as the Horde's primary quest hub and lore guide for entering the depths of Blackfathom Deeps from Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="Je'neu demonstrates how Darkspear trolls have embraced the spiritual paths of the Earthen Ring alongside their tauren and orc allies."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","je'neu sancrea","jeneu","twilight's hammer","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:6564","quest:6563","quest:6922","quest:824"},src={"Je'neu Sancrea"}}
E["npc:lady-sarevess"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Sarevess",z="blackfathom",s="Lady Sarevess is a twisted naga sorceress dwelling within the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, where she dabbles in dark sorceries.",h="Lady Sarevess is a twisted naga sorceress dwelling within the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, where she...",sec={{t="A Grotto in the Deeps",b="Within the Pool of Ask'ar, Lady Sarevess conducts her rituals in a flooded grotto of the ruined temple. A very twisted spellcaster, she dabbles in dark magic while the Twilight's Hammer cultists who also haunt the sunken temple pursue their own worship deeper in the cavern.",sp=0},{t="Sorcery of the Tides",b="Much like a sea witch of the deep oceans, Sarevess commands elemental currents and crackling arcs of lightning. Surrounded by loyal naga sentinels and summoned water elementals, she fiercely defends her sanctuary against any intruders who threaten her dark work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Sarevess?",a="Lady Sarevess is a naga spellcaster who has taken up residence within the subterranean Pool of Ask'ar inside Blackfathom Deeps. She is a very twisted spellcaster who dabbles in dark magic.",al={"who is sarevess","sarevess lore","lady sarevess backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Lady Sarevess be found?",a="She makes her lair in the Pool of Ask'ar, a flooded chamber situated in the early reaches of the Blackfathom Deeps temple complex along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"sarevess location","where is lady sarevess","pool of askar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What powers does Lady Sarevess command?",a="Drawing upon the traditions of naga sea witches, Sarevess wields powerful water and elemental magic, particularly violent bursts of forked lightning, to strike down anyone who enters her cove.",al={"sarevess magic","sarevess abilities"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Lady Sarevess on?",a="Lady Sarevess serves her own naga kin rather than the Alliance or the Horde. A very twisted spellcaster, she lairs in the flooded Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps and fiercely defends her grotto against any intruder.",al={"lady sarevess faction","who does sarevess serve","sarevess allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Lady Sarevess want?",a="Sarevess seeks to expand her mastery over twisted magical arts, conducting dark rituals in her flooded grotto deep within Blackfathom Deeps and striking down any intruder who disturbs her work.",al={"what is sarevess doing","lady sarevess goal","sarevess purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Lady Sarevess here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lady Sarevess has claimed the Pool of Ask'ar, a flooded grotto in the ruined temple of Blackfathom Deeps, as her lair. There she dabbles in dark magic, guarded by naga sentinels and summoned water elementals.",al={"why is lady sarevess in bfd","sarevess blackfathom deeps why","why is sarevess here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Lady Sarevess tied to?",a="Sarevess is tied to the naga who infest the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, commanding loyal naga sentinels and summoned water elementals in her grotto. The Twilight's Hammer cultists who also haunt the sunken temple pursue their own worship deeper in the cavern.",al={"sarevess allies","who does sarevess work with","sarevess twilight hammer"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins Lady Sarevess inhabits were once a sacred temple of Elune. Seeing her twisted naga kin defile the waters of Ask'ar is a bitter reminder of the Sundering.",["class:Mage"]="Sarevess demonstrates how highborne magical practices degenerated into raw, chaotic lightning and tidal sorcery under centuries of oceanic corruption."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","lady sarevess","naga","pool of ask'ar","sarevess","sea witch","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","topic:old-god"},src={"Lady Sarevess"}}
E["npc:lorgus-jett"] = {t="npc",n="Lorgus Jett",z="blackfathom",s="Lorgus Jett is a human member of the Twilight's Hammer cult operating within the flooded corridors of Blackfathom Deeps. Wandering the Moonshrine Ruins, he serves as a ruthless commander in the cult's service to the Old Gods. Horde leaders have singled him out as a primary target to disrupt the cult's encroaching presence along the Ashenvale coast.",h="Lorgus Jett is a human member of the Twilight's Hammer cult operating within the flooded corridors of...",sec={{t="A Defiler in the Ruins",b="While many members of the Twilight's Hammer working under Blackfathom Deeps hail from orcish or tauren lineages, Lorgus Jett stands out as a human in the deep recesses of ancient night elf ruins. Roaming anywhere between the upper Moonshrine Ruins and the cavernous tunnels beyond the murloc defiler Gelihast, Jett coordinates the cult's dark rituals and violent ambitions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lorgus Jett?",a="Lorgus Jett is a human operative of the Twilight's Hammer cult stationed inside Blackfathom Deeps. He oversees cult activities within the Moonshrine Ruins and serves the Old Gods.",al={"lorgus jett lore","who is lorgus","lorgus jett background"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Lorgus Jett be found in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lorgus Jett has a variable patrol area within the Moonshrine Ruins. He can appear near the earliest clusters of Twilight cultists or farther along in the flooded passages just past Gelihast's shrine.",al={"lorgus jett location","where is lorgus jett","find lorgus jett"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde want Lorgus Jett dead?",a="The Horde seeks his death through the mission 'Allegiance to the Old Gods.' His presence in Ashenvale threatens regional stability and represents an insidious alliance dedicated to unleashing ancient, world-ending entities.",al={"why kill lorgus","allegiance to the old gods quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does a human use shamanistic powers?",a="The Twilight's Hammer communes directly with chaotic elemental forces and Old Gods rather than traditional ancestral spirits, allowing non-traditional races like humans to wield elemental devastation.",al={"lorgus jett magic","human shaman lorgus"},it="power"},{q="What is Lorgus Jett's connection to Gelihast?",a="Both dwell in the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, united in their servitude to the dark powers sleeping beneath the sea, with Jett frequently patrolling the corridors beyond Gelihast's altar.",al={"lorgus and gelihast","gelihast connection"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Lorgus Jett on?",a="Lorgus Jett serves the Twilight's Hammer, the apocalyptic cult dedicated to the Old Gods. Though a human, he has abandoned his kin to align himself with the dark ritualists and elemental forces congregating within the forgotten depths of Ashenvale.",al={"lorgus jett faction","who does lorgus jett serve","what faction is lorgus jett"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="He lurks within the subterranean Moonshrine Ruins alongside his fellow cultists, carrying out the will of the Twilight's Hammer. Deep within the ancient elven temple, the cult tends to dark horrors and venerates the ancient powers stirring beneath the waters.",al={"why is lorgus jett in bfd","lorgus jett purpose blackfathom","why is lorgus jett here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Jett wields the elements not in harmony or reverence, but through the corrupted, violent methods taught by the Twilight's Hammer.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking down Lorgus Jett fulfills an urgent request to sever the leadership of the Twilight's Hammer festering beneath the Ashenvale shore.",["race:Human"]="Seeing a human so far west in Kalimdor serving cosmic terrors is a chilling reminder of how far the corruption of the Twilight's Hammer has reached."},kw={"allegiance to the old gods","blackfathom deeps","lorgus jett","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:6564","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:gelihast","topic:old-god"},src={"Lorgus Jett"}}
E["npc:old-serra-kis"] = {t="npc",n="Old Serra'kis",z="blackfathom",s="Old Serra'kis is an ancient, massive threshadon dwelling in the submerged subterranean waters of Blackfathom Deeps. While the invading Twilight's Hammer culled much of the temple's aquatic life for provisions, this enormous beast proved entirely lethal to any who attempted to hunt it.",h="Old Serra'kis is an ancient, massive threshadon dwelling in the submerged subterranean waters of Blackfathom...",sec={{t="Unconquered in the Depths",b="When the Twilight's Hammer cultists descended upon the sunken Moonshrine Ruins, they slaughtered the native wildlife beneath the waters for sustenance. Yet beneath the Moonshrine Sanctum, one primeval creature refused to become prey. Old Serra'kis, the largest threshadon in the sunken temple, made short work of any cultist brazen enough to spear him. Eventually, the hunters abandoned their efforts, leaving the ancient carnivore undisturbed in his watery domain.",sp=0},{t="A Hidden Threat",b="Reaching Old Serra'kis requires plunging deep beneath the temple floor into a flooded cavern beneath the ruins. Lacking air pockets, the cave itself is as deadly as the beast within. Those who corner him find that Serra'kis possesses an unnatural shadow-leeching resilience, draining the life from his attackers while sustaining his own vitality in the murky darkness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Old Serra'kis?",a="Old Serra'kis is a massive, ancient threshadon—a long-necked, aquatic reptile native to the lakes and coastal waters of Azeroth.",al={"what is serrakis","is serrakis a hydra","serrakis creature type"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the Twilight's Hammer kill him?",a="The cult slaughtered most aquatic life beneath the Moonshrine Ruins for food, but Serra'kis was too powerful and cunning. Cultists who persisted in attempting to hunt him inevitably ended up as his meals instead, leading the cult to avoid his cave entirely.",al={"why is serrakis still alive","twilights hammer serrakis"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Old Serra'kis located?",a="He lurks in a submerged cavern beneath the water surrounding the Moonshrine Sanctum within Blackfathom Deeps. Swimmers must dive under the ruins into an airless pool to encounter him.",al={"how to find serrakis","serrakis location","where is old serrakis"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What makes fighting him dangerous?",a="Beyond fighting entirely underwater without natural pockets of air, Old Serra'kis leeches shadow energy from all nearby foes to heal his own wounds throughout combat.",al={"serrakis abilities","how to beat serrakis"},it="danger"},{q="Does Serra'kis serve the Twilight's Hammer?",a="No. Unlike other beasts corrupted or trained by the cult, Old Serra'kis remains a completely untamed wild predator defending his subterranean lair.",al={"is serrakis a cultist pet","who controls serrakis"},it="side"},{q="Can you breathe during the battle with Serra'kis?",a="His enclosed cave offers no ceiling air pockets, forcing underwater fighters to either manage their breath, use magical water-breathing aid, or kite the beast out toward open water.",al={"drowning serrakis","breath underwater serrakis"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why is Old Serra'kis feared?",a="Old Serra'kis is feared as the largest and deadliest predator lurking beneath the Moonshrine Ruins. When the Twilight's Hammer cultists arrived and began harvesting the local aquatic wildlife for sustenance, Serra'kis proved entirely uncatchable. Any hunters who dared pursue him into the submerged caves inevitably met a gruesome death, earning the giant threshadon an untouchable reputation among the cult.",al={"serrakis reputation","why is serrakis famous","why fear serrakis"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the wild will find Aquatic Form indispensable when diving into the lightless pool to confront this prehistoric predator.",["class:Warlock"]="A warlock's ability to bestow Unending Breath turns an otherwise deadly, airless subterranean ambush into a manageable fight.",["class:Shaman"]="Water Breathing spells granted by spiritual communion with the elements ensure your companions don't drown while grappling with the ancient thresher."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","forgotten pool","moonshrine sanctum","old serrakis","serrakis","threshadon","twilight's hammer","underwater boss"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","subzone:forgotten-pool","topic:twilight-s-hammer","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic"},src={"Old Serra'kis"}}
E["npc:scout-thaelrid"] = {t="npc",n="Argent Guard Thaelrid",z="blackfathom",s="Argent Guard Thaelrid is a wounded night elf scout sent by the Argent Dawn into the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Trapped near the Pool of Ask'ar, he bears witness to the dark alliance taking root between the naga and the Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="Argent Guard Thaelrid is a wounded night elf scout sent by the Argent Dawn into the submerged ruins of...",sec={{t="Eyes of the Argent Dawn",b="When strange reports trickled out of the Zoram Strand concerning foul rites deep beneath the sea, the Argent Dawn took interest. Dedicated to watching for rising evils and unnatural corruption across Azeroth, the order dispatched Scout Thaelrid to slip inside Blackfathom Deeps. His mission was simple: assess the depth of the threat, observe the movements within the flooded temple, and report back so the Dawn could decide where aid was most desperately needed.",sp=0},{t="A Grasping Darkness",b="Thaelrid quickly discovered that the rumors fell far short of the horrific reality. The subterranean ruins harbor an unholy pact between savage naga and the doomsday zealots of the Twilight's Hammer. Deep within the halls, cultists under the command of Twilight Lord Kelris perform blood sacrifices to feed the hydra Aku'mai, bargaining with ancient terrors for dark power. Before Thaelrid could deliver this warning to the surface, he was grievously wounded and cut off, leaving him stranded near the Pool of Ask'ar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="He is a night elf operative serving the Argent Dawn. He was tasked with infiltrating Blackfathom Deeps along Ashenvale's coast to gather intelligence on the sinister forces gathering below.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","thaelrid background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Thaelrid trapped inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="While reconnoitering the cavernous temple, Thaelrid was discovered and grievously wounded by the denizens within. Unable to fight his way back to the surface alone, he took shelter near the Pool of Ask'ar.",al={"why is he stuck","how did he get wounded","why is thaelrid dying"},it="why_here"},{q="What did Thaelrid discover in the depths?",a="Thaelrid investigates the Twilight's Hammer activity in Blackfathom Deeps, where the cult's presence threatens the ancient temple and those who enter it.",al={"what did thaelrid find","what are the cultists doing","blackfathom secrets"}},{q="Who does Thaelrid work for?",a="He belongs to the Argent Dawn, the neutral organization dedicated to combating corruption, evil, and apocalyptic threats throughout Azeroth regardless of faction lines.",al={"thaelrid faction","is thaelrid argent dawn","is thaelrid alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Thaelrid ask adventurers to do?",a="Unable to leave his refuge, Thaelrid asks courageous adventurers to put an end to the butchery by slaying Twilight Lord Kelris, retrieving the cult leader's head to prove the threat is broken.",al={"thaelrid quest","blackfathom villainy quest","what does he want"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Thaelrid be found?",a="He rests injured in a secluded alcove near the Pool of Ask'ar, an area just past the flooded preliminary caverns of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is thaelrid","thaelrid location","pool of askar scout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid tied to?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid answers directly to the Argent Dawn. Charged with keeping watch against encroaching evils across Azeroth, the order dispatched him into the submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps to verify alarming reports regarding the Twilight's Hammer cult and their newfound naga allies.",al={"thaelrid ties","who does thaelrid answer to","scout thaelrid argent dawn"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing sacred, ancient temple grounds like Blackfathom defiled by naga and doomsday cults is a bitter outrage; Thaelrid represents their people's vigil over Kalimdor's deepest wounds.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts sent into Ashenvale follow up on Thaelrid's disappearance, eager to maintain the safety of the Zoram Strand and support the neutral work of the Argent Dawn.",["faction:Horde"]="Though Thaelrid is a night elf, his allegiance is to the Argent Dawn, meaning any adventurer willing to strike at the Twilight's Hammer and cleanse the cavern can aid him."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","pool of ask'ar","scout thaelrid","thaelrid","twilight lord kelris"},rel={"quest:1198","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","topic:argent-dawn","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Scout Thaelrid"}}
E["npc:tsunaman"] = {t="npc",n="Tsunaman",z="blackfathom",s="Tsunaman is a sentient water elemental stationed at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. Acting as an agent of the Tribunal of the Tides, he watches over the elemental currents of Kalimdor and rallies Horde adventurers to confront corrupting forces.",h="Tsunaman is a sentient water elemental stationed at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="Agent of the Tides",b="Dwelling near the path leading from Sun Rock Retreat down into the Charred Vale, Tsunaman serves the Tribunal of the Tides, high-ranking servants aligned with the Tidehunter, Neptulon. Rather than showing mindless hostility to mortal travelers, he cooperates with the Horde to monitor elemental unrest throughout Kalimdor, particularly the disturbances rippling out of the submerged caverns of Blackfathom Deeps.",sp=0},{t="Hatred of Flame",b="True to his elemental nature, Tsunaman harbors an instinctive, visceral hatred for fire in all forms. He constantly fumes over the nearby burning landscapes of the Charred Vale and elemental fire incursions. In camp, his animosity is so petty and unyielding that he regularly marches over to nearby cooking fires and campfires just to smack them out with a heavy fist of water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tsunaman?",a="Tsunaman is a water elemental located at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves as an emissary for the Tribunal of the Tides, watching elemental conflicts in Kalimdor and seeking help against unnatural disturbances.",al={"who is tsunaman","tsunaman lore","what is tsunaman"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tsunaman attack the campfire?",a="Tsunaman despises fire elementals and the concept of fire itself. Driven by elemental rivalry, he will periodically stomp over to campfires lit by travelers in Sun Rock Retreat and extinguish them with a watery strike.",al={"tsunaman punching fire","why does tsunaman hit fire","water elemental campfire"}},{q="What is the Tribunal of the Tides?",a="The Tribunal of the Tides is an order of powerful elemental lieutenants serving Neptulon the Tidehunter, the Elemental Lord of water. They oversee aquatic domains and react to disruptions in the world's waters.",al={"tribunal of the tides","who does tsunaman serve"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Tsunaman interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps has become polluted by twilight cultists and dark forces corrupting the native water spirits. Tsunaman enlists Horde adventurers to delve into the sunken temple and quell the chaos disrupting the waters.",al={"tsunaman blackfathom","trouble in the deeps"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Tsunaman on?",a="Tsunaman does not answer to the mortal races of the Horde or the Alliance. He serves the elemental powers of water, specifically the Tribunal of the Tides who stand as high-ranking lieutenants of Neptulon the Tidehunter. While he tolerates visitors at Sun Rock Retreat and enlists adventurers against common foes, his true loyalty lies entirely with the watery depths and his elemental brethren.",al={"tsunaman faction","who does tsunaman serve","tsunaman allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Tsunaman want?",a="Tsunaman is driven by the ancient elemental struggle. He seeks the eradication of rival fire elementals and despises flame in all its forms, regularly lashing out at even simple campfires. Furthermore, he works to advance the interests of the Tribunal of the Tides by recruiting capable mortals to address dark disturbances within aquatic sanctuaries like the Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"tsunaman goals","what is tsunaman trying to do","tsunaman desires"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Tsunaman here in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Tsunaman stations himself along the trail leading out from Sun Rock Retreat toward the scorched lands of the Charred Vale. Positioned here on behalf of the Tribunal of the Tides, he watches the nearby elemental conflicts unfolding across the Stonetalon Mountains and reaches out to passing adventurers who can strike out against encroaching fiery adversaries or venture into troubled subterranean waters.",al={"why is tsunaman in stonetalon","tsunaman sun rock retreat reason","why did tsunaman come here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For shamans striving to understand and commune with the elements, Tsunaman offers a rare chance to speak directly with an emissary of the Tidehunter's court.",["faction:Horde"]="Tsunaman treats the Horde at Sun Rock Retreat as convenient allies against elemental imbalance and cultist intrusion in Kalimdor's waters."},kw={"charred vale","neptulon","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tribunal of the tides","trouble in the deeps","tsunaman","water elemental"},rel={"quest:6562","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","zone:blackfathom","subzone:charred-vale"},src={"Tsunaman"}}
E["npc:twilight-lord-kelris"] = {t="npc",n="Twilight Lord Kelris",z="blackfathom",s="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc warlock and high-ranking leader within the Twilight's Hammer cult operating deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. From his perch in the Moonshrine Sanctum, he leads dark rituals and tends to the primordial hydra Aku'mai, aiming to usher in a reign of cosmic chaos.",h="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc warlock and high-ranking leader within the Twilight's Hammer cult operating...",sec={{t="Herald of the Void",b="Twilight Lord Kelris directs the cultists of the Twilight's Hammer who seized the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. For years, Kelris slipped through the grasp of watchful eyes in Darnassus, evading the Argent Dawn and earning a grim reputation: whenever ancient malice stirred across Kalimdor, Kelris was suspected of orchestrating it. Rather than serving warlords or clans, this orc has pledged himself entirely to the Old Gods, seeking to unmake mortal civilization and return Azeroth to a state of absolute, primordial chaos.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of the Beast",b="Within the Moonshrine Sanctum, Kelris oversees the worship and cultivation of Aku'mai, a vicious three-headed hydra considered a herald and favored pet of the Old Gods. Convinced that raising this abomination will unlock his own immortality and signal the return of his masters, Kelris personally monitors its growth. To sate the creature's bottomless hunger, he feeds it captured sacrifices and even disobedient cultists from his own ranks.",sp=0},{t="Dark Trance and Slumber",b="Kelris commands potent shadow magic capable of seizing minds and plunging intruders into deep, unnatural sleep. He conducts constant prayers before a corrupted altar surrounded by candles that channel dark energies. Those attempting to strike down Kelris must not only defeat the cult leader, but also navigate the latent horrors that stir once his ritualistic vigil is broken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc sorcerer who commands the Twilight's Hammer presence in Blackfathom Deeps. He coordinates cult activity throughout the sunken temple and is deeply devoted to the Old Gods.",al={"kelris lore","who is kelris","kelris background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn hunting Kelris?",a="The Argent Dawn views Kelris as an elusive instigator of malice throughout Kalimdor. Though he was once believed dead or missing, his hand was discovered behind numerous dark plots across the continent, making his elimination a priority.",al={"argent dawn kelris","why kill kelris","blackfathom villainy reason"},it="fame"},{q="What is Kelris doing with the hydra Aku'mai?",a="Kelris believes the three-headed hydra Aku'mai is a direct herald of the Old Gods and his path to eternal life. He personally nurtures the monster, offering it live sacrifices to fuel its growth.",al={"kelris and akumai","why is kelris feeding akumai"},it="wants"},{q="What happens after Kelris is defeated?",a="Behind Kelris sits an altar with four ceremonial candles. Lighting these candles unbinds the sanctum's protective wards, summoning waves of Aku'mai's servants and opening the sealed gate to the beast's lair.",al={"kelris candles","altar of kelris","moonshrine candles"},sp=1},{q="What powers does Kelris use in combat?",a="Kelris wields potent shadow spells, mental domination, and a magical slumber that can incapacitate his enemies while his dark rites continue.",al={"kelris abilities","kelris spells"},it="power"},{q="Who is Bashana Runetotem?",a="Bashana Runetotem is an ally investigating the corruption in Blackfathom Deeps who warns adventurers of Kelris's obsession with Old God worship and his desire to plunge the world back into primeval chaos.",al={"bashana runetotem kelris","tauren hunter kelris"}},{q="Whose side is Twilight Lord Kelris on?",a="Kelris leads the local cell of the Twilight's Hammer cult. He serves neither the Horde nor the Alliance, dedicating his life entirely to the worship and service of the ancient Old Gods and the return of primordial chaos to Azeroth.",al={"kelris faction","who does kelris serve","twilight lord kelris allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Twilight Lord Kelris here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Kelris established his sanctum in the sunken ruins to secretly commune with the Old Gods and nurture the massive hydra Aku'mai. Convinced the beast is a harbinger of his dark masters' return, he oversees its growth from within the Moonshrine Sanctum, far away from watchful eyes.",al={"why is kelris in bfd","kelris blackfathom purpose","why did kelris come here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris tied to?",a="Beyond commanding the Twilight's Hammer cultists lurking in the cavern, Kelris is bound directly to the dread hydra Aku'mai, which he feeds and grooms. He also maintains ties to the Old Gods he worships, carrying out their dark designs across Kalimdor.",al={"kelris allies","who does kelris work with","kelris connections"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Argent Dawn operating from Darnassus seeks the end of Kelris's elusive career of stirring dark cults and terror across northern Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Elders and shamans view Kelris as a cautionary abomination—an orc who abandoned the elements and ancestral spirits to grovel before ancient cosmic horrors.",["class:Warlock"]="While typical warlocks barter with demons of the Burning Legion, Kelris demonstrates the dark, trance-induced shadow magic born from yielding to Old God whispers.",["race:NightElf"]="Kelris's blasphemous rituals actively despoil the sacred Moonshrine Sanctum, desecrating an ancient elven temple dedicated to Elune."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","kelris","moonshrine sanctum","old gods","twilight lord","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:1200","npc:aku-mai","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:argent-dawn","npc:bashana-runetotem"},src={"Twilight Lord Kelris"}}
E["quest:1198"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Thaelrid",z="blackfathom",s="In Search of Thaelrid is an Alliance reconnaissance mission dispatched from Darnassus on behalf of the Argent Dawn. Dawnwatcher Shaedlass tasks adventurers with venturing into the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps to locate a missing scout who vanished while investigating a dangerous alliance between naga and cultists. It represents an early encounter with the reach of the Argent Dawn beyond their typical northern vigil.",h="In Search of Thaelrid is an Alliance reconnaissance mission dispatched from Darnassus on behalf of the Argent...",sec={{t="Eyes in Darnassus",b="Though the Argent Dawn is most renowned for holding the line against the Scourge in the plague-ridden ruins of Lordaeron, its vigilance extends across Kalimdor. Stationed within Darnassus, Dawnwatcher Shaedlass gathers whispers and intelligence on unnatural threats emerging across the world. When unsettling reports arose that sea-dwelling naga and the doomsday zealots of the Twilight's Hammer had forged a pact within the flooded chambers of Blackfathom Deeps along the Ashenvale shore, the order recognized the potential catastrophe.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Scout",b="To assess the veracity of these coastal rumors, Shaedlass dispatched Argent Guard Thaelrid to quietly infiltrate the subterranean caverns. Weeks passed without word, leaving the Dawnwatcher in the dark with his other scouts committed to separate operations. Fearing that Thaelrid had either fallen in battle or been captured by the dark powers dwelling beneath the waves, he enlists seasoned travelers brave enough to breach Blackfathom Deeps and bring him back alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Argent Dawn interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Argent Dawn monitors all existential, corrupting threats across Azeroth, not just the undead of the Eastern Kingdoms. The prospect of ancient naga collaborating with fanatical cultists of the Twilight's Hammer within Kalimdor represents a destabilizing evil that demands their attention.",al={"why argent dawn here","argent dawn blackfathom","argent dawn naga"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is an Argent Dawn operative stationed within the night elf capital of Darnassus. His primary duty is information gathering, identifying where the order's aid is urgently required and dispatching investigators to evaluate regional crises.",al={"who is shaedlass","quest giver shaedlass","dawnwatcher shaedlass role"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid is an operative of the Argent Dawn sent to conduct reconnaissance on Blackfathom Deeps. His mission was to determine the true strength and intent of the cultists and naga residing within the drowned caverns.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","missing scout thaelrid"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thaelrid be found?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid has successfully infiltrated the subterranean depths of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, though he remains isolated deep within the caverns awaiting reinforcements.",al={"thaelrid location","where is thaelrid","find thaelrid bfd"},gp=true},{q="What happens after finding Thaelrid?",a="Upon being located, Thaelrid reveals the full, insidious nature of the ritual underway inside the ruins, immediately directing adventurers toward a strike against the cult's leadership in the quest Blackfathom Villainy.",al={"what comes next","followup to thaelrid","next quest after thaelrid"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Horde players take this mission?",a="The assignment is given by Dawnwatcher Shaedlass in Darnassus and is aimed at Alliance adventurers. Horde adventurers can also accept it if they reach him.",al={"horde in search of thaelrid","can horde do this quest","horde thaelrid"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dawnwatcher Shaedlass want you to find Thaelrid?",a="Shaedlass gathers intelligence for the Argent Dawn to monitor growing evils across Kalimdor. Weeks ago, he dispatched Argent Guard Thaelrid to investigate disturbing rumors regarding an alliance between the naga and the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. With no word returned from him, he fears the worst and needs to confirm both the status of the scout and the truth behind the sinister plot taking root along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"why find thaelrid","shaedlass motive","why send to blackfathom deeps"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Shaedlass send an adventurer instead of his own scouts?",a="The Argent Dawn's presence in Darnassus is thin, and Shaedlass notes that all of his other scouts are fully preoccupied with their own urgent missions across the land. With Thaelrid missing and no available agents left to spare, he must rely on capable and willing adventurers to enter the treacherous depths on his behalf.",al={"why me in search of thaelrid","why not send argent dawn scouts"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This mission marks one of the earliest opportunities for Alliance adventurers to establish goodwill and service alongside the Argent Dawn.",["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of the ancient Temple of Elune within Blackfathom Deeps makes assisting the Argent Dawn an urgent matter of recovering sacred night elven heritage.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins aligned with the Argent Dawn recognize Thaelrid's solitary vigil as a solemn duty to protect the world from creeping shadow and corruption."},kw={"argent dawn","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","darnassus","naga","shaedlass","thaelrid","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:dawnwatcher-shaedlass","zone:blackfathom","quest:1200","topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","zone:ashenvale","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga"},m={start="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass",["end"]="Argent Guard Thaelrid",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1198},src={"In Search of Thaelrid"}}
E["quest:1199"] = {t="quest",n="Twilight Falls",z="blackfathom",s="Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus calls upon Alliance champions to strike at the Twilight's Hammer cultists gathered within Blackfathom Deeps. The dark cult has allied with serpent-like naga to occupy the sunken night elf temple along the Ashenvale coast. By gathering pendants from the fallen cultists, adventurers strike a blow against their insidious plans to awaken ancient evils.",h="Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus calls upon Alliance champions to strike at the Twilight's Hammer cultists...",sec={{t="A Sanctum Defiled",b="Beneath the rugged cliffs of the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale lie the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Once a sacred night elf temple dedicated to Elune and home to a powerful moonwell, it was shattered and plunged into the depths during the Sundering. Today, the sacred waters have turned putrid and foul, overrun by bloodthirsty naga and fanatic cultists who venerate forces far darker than the sea.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Old Gods",b="The Twilight's Hammer is an apocalyptic cult devoted to the chaotic Old Gods, seeking to bring about the return of their primordial patrons and cover the world in madness and ruin. Reports reaching Darnassus confirm that these madmen have joined hands with the naga inhabiting Blackfathom Deeps. Deep within the submerged halls, they conduct blasphemous rituals, using the sunken temple's tainted waters to feed their dark masters' resurgence.",sp=0},{t="The Vigil of the Argent Dawn",b="Stationed in Darnassus, Argent Guard Manados represents the Argent Dawn's vigilance against all scourges that threaten Azeroth. Recognizing that the depravity within Blackfathom Deeps could unleash horrors upon all civilized races, the order offers recognition and aid to any heroes willing to descend into the flooded labyrinth, cull the cultists, and pry the Twilight Pendants from their necks as proof of their downfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Manados?",a="Argent Guard Manados is an emissary of the Argent Dawn stationed in Darnassus. Acting as the eyes and ears of his order in Kalimdor, he monitors malevolent cults and dark forces that threaten the realm, enlisting adventurers to eradicate them.",al={"manados","who gives twilight falls","argent guard manados location"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn concerned about Blackfathom Deeps?",a="While the Argent Dawn is best known for fighting the Scourge in Lordaeron, their charter encompasses confronting any existential, unnatural evil. The resurgence of Old God worship and the alliance between cultists and naga in Kalimdor represents a global catastrophe if left unchecked.",al={"why argent dawn darnassus","argent dawn blackfathom"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Twilight's Hammer?",a="The Twilight's Hammer is a fanatical doomsday cult that worships the Old Gods—chaotic, primordial entities imprisoned beneath the earth long ago. Cultists believe in hastening an apocalyptic end where their shadowy masters rise again to remake the world in terror and madness.",al={"twilight hammer cult","who are twilight's hammer","twilights hammer"},it="target"},{q="What were the Twilight Pendants used for?",a="The Twilight Pendants are dark talismans worn by members of the Twilight's Hammer. Symbolizing their allegiance to the chaotic entities they worship, the Argent Dawn collects them as verifiable proof that a cultist has been slain and neutralized.",al={"twilight pendant lore","what are twilight pendants"},it="item"},{q="What was Blackfathom Deeps originally?",a="Long before its corruption, Blackfathom Deeps was a magnificent night elven temple dedicated to the moon goddess Elune. It was renowned for housing a profoundly potent moonwell before the Great Sundering cracked the earth and submerged its halls beneath the sea.",al={"blackfathom history","bfd temple history","blackfathom moonwell"},it="place"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer working with the naga?",a="Both the naga and the Twilight's Hammer share deep, dark allegiances to the chaotic forces of the deep. Within Blackfathom Deeps, their cooperation allows the cultists safe access to ancient submerged chambers while the naga benefit from the cult's vile sorceries and sacrificial rites.",al={"naga cultists alliance","bfd naga alliance"},it="allies"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The desecration of a sacred temple and moonwell by creeping void-worshipers and naga is a direct affront to Elune and the ancestral lands of Ashenvale.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Twilight's Hammer poses an encroaching peril just south of Darkshore, making the purge of Blackfathom Deeps essential to securing northern Kalimdor.",["class:Paladin"]="As champions of the Holy Light aligned with orders like the Argent Dawn, paladins view the Twilight's Hammer's depraved Old God worship as an abomination demanding righteous cleansing.",["class:Priest"]="Priests are keenly attuned to the perversion of the temple's once-sacred moonwell and the maddening, shadowy whispers driving the cultists deeper into madness."},kw={"argent dawn","argent guard manados","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","darnassus","manados","naga","old gods","twilight falls","twilight pendant","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:argent-guard-manados","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","topic:naga","zone:darnassus","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Argent Guard Manados",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1199,ri={"Twilight Pendant"}},src={"Twilight Falls (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1200"] = {t="quest",n="Blackfathom Villainy",z="blackfathom",s="Blackfathom Villainy is an Alliance task given by Argent Guard Thaelrid deep within the ruined subterranean temple of Blackfathom Deeps. To halt the horrific sacrifices fueling an ancient horror, heroes are tasked with executing the cult leader Twilight Lord Kelris and bringing proof back to the Argent Dawn in Darnassus.",h="Blackfathom Villainy is an Alliance task given by Argent Guard Thaelrid deep within the ruined subterranean...",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="The flooded cavern now known as Blackfathom Deeps was once a pristine subterranean temple dedicated to Elune. That sacred past was shattered when the corruption of an ancient Old God seeped up through the rock, spoiling the temple's Moon Well and releasing Aku'mai, a voracious servant of that primordial darkness. In the wake of this defilement, the Twilight's Hammer cult forged an unholy alliance with local naga, turning holy halls into a den of ritual murder.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Guard's Plea",b="Argent Guard Thaelrid ventured into Blackfathom Deeps on behalf of his order, only to be grievously wounded and drained of his strength. Stranded amidst enemies, Thaelrid realizes he cannot finish his mission alone. He implores any brave Alliance travelers who reach him to strike down Twilight Lord Kelris, the sinister cultist orchestrating the sacrifice of innocents to Aku'mai in exchange for dark power.",sp=0},{t="Justice in Darnassus",b="Presenting the severed head of Kelris to Dawnwatcher Selgorm at the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus finally closes a long and troubling hunt. The Argent Dawn had feared Kelris was dead or lost to the shadows, given his recurring involvement whenever dark forces stirred in Kalimdor. Slaying him secures a vital victory against the cult's designs in Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="Thaelrid is an operative of the Argent Dawn sent to investigate the growing shadow within Blackfathom Deeps. Grievously wounded in the depths, his depleted strength forces him to recruit passing adventurers to stop Kelris.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","argent guard"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Twilight Lord Kelris being targeted?",a="Kelris is the leader of the Twilight's Hammer cultists inhabiting Blackfathom Deeps. He has been systematically sacrificing innocent captives to Aku'mai, a foul beast linked to the Old Gods, in exchange for malevolent power.",al={"who is kelris","why kill kelris","twilight lord kelris"},it="target"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm?",a="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is an Argent Dawn representative stationed on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. He oversees the order's efforts to thwart encroaching corruptions across northern Kalimdor.",al={"selgorm darnassus","who is selgorm","argent dawn darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="What is the history of Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Before it became a sunken lair of monsters and cultists, the caverns housed a great night elven temple dedicated to the goddess Elune. It fell into ruin after an Old God's malice bled upward and fouled its sacred Moon Well.",al={"bfd history","what was blackfathom deeps","temple of elune bfd"},it="history"},{q="Who is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous, hydra-like servant of an Old God that crawled forth from the tainted waters beneath Blackfathom Deeps. The Twilight's Hammer reveres the creature, feeding it captives to gain dark blessings.",al={"what is akumai","aku'mai lore","akumai beast"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer and naga working together?",a="Both factions share an allegiance to dark, ancient masters tied to the depths. In Blackfathom Deeps, they have allied to claim the ruined temple grounds and commune with Aku'mai.",al={"naga cultists alliance","why are naga in bfd","twilight hammer and naga"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Thaelrid want Twilight Lord Kelris slain?",a="Thaelrid has uncovered that Twilight Lord Kelris and his cultists are sacrificing innocent captives to Aku'mai, a servant of an Old God, in exchange for dark power. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, Thaelrid is dedicated to halting such evil and ending the gruesome ritual slaughter taking place within the ruined temple.",al={"thaelrid motive","why does thaelrid want kelris dead","why kill kelris"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Head of Kelris for?",a="The head serves as undeniable proof of the cult leader's demise. Dawnwatcher Selgorm and the Argent Dawn believed Kelris was dead or missing after years of elusive villainy across Kalimdor. Bringing his head to Selgorm in Darnassus confirms that his reign of terror and blood sacrifices have finally come to an end.",al={"head of kelris","why do i need kelris's head","what to do with kelris head"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why can't Argent Guard Thaelrid slay Kelris himself?",a="Thaelrid is trapped deep within the flooded ruins, captive and completely exhausted. Having lost his strength and suffering under the cultists' imprisonment, he is physically unable to fight his way out, let alone strike down Kelris on his own. He relies on you to finish the mission in his stead.",al={"why doesn't thaelrid fight kelris","why does thaelrid need me","can thaelrid kill kelris"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Avenging the defilement of an ancient temple of Elune and cleansing its poisoned Moon Well strikes directly at the heart of kaldorei heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="By aiding the Argent Dawn against Kelris, the Alliance helps protect the vulnerable borders of Ashenvale from insidious cult infiltration.",["class:Paladin"]="Answering the call of the Argent Dawn to slay a cultist who sacrifices innocents to primordial horrors is the very definition of holy retribution.",["class:Priest"]="Stopping Kelris brings an end to the blasphemous desecration of consecrated waters once held holy in devotion to the divine."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","blackfathom","darnassus","deeps","elune","kelris","moon well","selgorm","thaelrid","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:twilight-lord-kelris","quest:1198","npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Argent Guard Thaelrid",["end"]="Dawnwatcher Selgorm",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1200,ri={"Head of Kelris"}},src={"Blackfathom Villainy (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:1275"] = {t="quest",n="Researching the Corruption",z="blackfathom",s="Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine seeks corrupted brain stems from the creatures infesting Blackfathom Deeps. Disturbed by reports of the blood elves dabbling in demonic magic across the sea, he hopes to study the physiological descent of the naga and satyr to foresee—and perhaps avert—another catastrophic elven mutation.",h="Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine seeks corrupted brain stems from the creatures infesting Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Warning from History",b="To the night elves of Kalimdor, the ruin of their ancient kin is a living memory etched into monsters. Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne succumbed to the allure of demonic energies, warping themselves into horned satyrs or drowning into serpentine naga. Watching the high elves rebrand themselves as blood elves and embrace dark magic strikes Gershala Nightwhisper not as a distant curiosity, but as history doomed to repeat itself.",sp=0},{t="Into the Deeps",b="Blackfathom Deeps serves as an ideal specimen ground for Gershala's grim inquiry. Hidden beneath the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, the subterranean temple ruins crawl with both satyr cultists and coiled naga. By sending an adventurer to harvest brain stems from both monstrosities, he hopes to dissect the biological link between arcane addiction, demonic corruption, and catastrophic bodily transformation.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Cure",b="While Gershala's methods are chillingly anatomical, his stated intent is preventative. He believes that deciphering the exact physiological mutations shared by satyrs and naga could yield the knowledge needed to pull the blood elves back from total damnation. Whether any research conducted in darkshore can truly sway the desperate elves of Quel'Thalas remains an open question.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gershala Nightwhisper care about the blood elves?",a="Gershala fears that the blood elves' flirtation with demonic powers will spawn another race of twisted monsters to menace Azeroth, just as past elven hubris gave rise to the satyrs and naga.",al={"why help blood elves","gershala blood elf connection","auberdine blood elves"},it="motive"},{q="Where do you gather the corrupted brain stems?",a="They are collected from the satyrs and naga dwelling within Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient temple complex buried along the Zoram Strand on the northwest coast of Ashenvale.",al={"where are brain stems","brain stem location","corrupt brain stem drop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does he specifically want satyr and naga samples?",a="Both the satyrs and the naga originated from elves who were warped by unnatural forces—satyrs through demonic bargains, and naga through the Sundering. Gershala wants to compare their brain mutations to map how elven physiology deteriorates under dark power.",al={"why satyr and naga","satyr naga connection"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who leads you to this task?",a="You can be directed to Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine via an introductory breadcrumb quest, 'The Corruption Abroad,' though he will also offer this investigation directly.",al={"prerequisite quest","corruption abroad connection"},it="origin"},{q="What does Gershala plan to do with the specimens?",a="He plans to study the physiological correlations between the two forms of corruption, hoping the resulting knowledge could help forestall the blood elves' descent into deeper monstrosity.",al={"brain stem study","gershala research goal"},it="item"},{q="Is Auberdine directly threatened by Blackfathom Deeps?",a="While Blackfathom Deeps lies just across the southern border in Ashenvale, the night elves of Auberdine monitor the entire coastal region for signs of escalating demonic and Twilight corruption.",al={"why auberdine cares","blackfathom deeps threat darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="Who are you sent against in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Gershala sends you against the satyrs and naga dwelling within Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale. Both species were once night elves before undergoing grotesque magical transformations—the satyrs warped by demonic corruption during the War of the Ancients, and the naga mutated by ancient dark powers beneath the sea. Now, both factions inhabit the submerged temple ruins.",al={"what enemies for researching corruption","who do i fight blackfathom deeps","researching the corruption targets"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, this research touches on the rawest wound in their history: the catastrophic degradation of their kin into the satyrs and naga who plague Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold an innate revulsion toward the satyrs, whose fel corruption defiles the natural dream and warps the land itself.",["class:Mage"]="Gershala's grim investigation is a stark reminder of the physical and spiritual costs of reckless, unchecked magical dependence.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps a wary eye on reports of the blood elves' descent into dark arts across the sea, dreading the emergence of a new demonic threat."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackfathom deeps","blood elves","corrupted brain stem","corruption abroad","gershala nightwhisper","naga","satyr"},rel={"npc:gershala-nightwhisper","quest:3765","zone:blackfathom","subzone:auberdine","topic:satyr","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Gershala Nightwhisper",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1275,ri={"Corrupted Brain Stem"}},src={"Researching the Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6561"] = {t="quest",n="Blackfathom Villainy",z="blackfathom",s="Blackfathom Villainy is an urgent plea delivered by a dying Argent Dawn crusader trapped inside Blackfathom Deeps. Horde adventurers are charged with putting an end to Twilight Lord Kelris, the cult leader orchestrating horrific blood sacrifices to an ancient monstrosity in the ruins below.",h="Blackfathom Villainy is an urgent plea delivered by a dying Argent Dawn crusader trapped inside Blackfathom...",sec={{t="A Desperate Last Stand",b="Drawn to the subterranean temple along the Ashenvale coast, the Argent Dawn scout Thaelrid discovered horrors far worse than simple naga incursions. Wounded and stripped of strength within the caverns, the night elf realizes he cannot finish his mission alone. Rather than letting his reconnaissance die with him, he turns to any passing Horde champions willing to strike at the dark leadership presiding over the sunken halls.",sp=0},{t="Sacrifices to the Deep",b="The target of the task is Twilight Lord Kelris, the head of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who have entrenched themselves within the ruined Temple of the Moon. Allied with the local naga, Kelris conducts dark rituals over the defiled Moon Well, feeding living captives to Aku'mai—a ravenous hydra and beast of the Old Gods—in a mad pursuit of cosmic power and primordial chaos.",sp=0},{t="Word to Thunder Bluff",b="Kelris was once thought dead or lost by the Argent Dawn, making confirmation of his demise vital. Rather than forcing heroes back into human lands, Thaelrid directs proof of the cult leader's death to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Bashana, deeply attuned to the natural balance of the Earthmother, honors the victory for extinguishing a foul corruption bent on dragging Kalimdor into primeval ruin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Kelris is the leader of the Twilight's Hammer cultists occupying Blackfathom Deeps. Believed by the Argent Dawn to have been dead or missing, he has instead been secretly gathering power by offering living sacrifices to the ancient hydra Aku'mai in the corrupted Moon Well.",al={"kelris","who is kelris","twilight lord kelris"},it="target"},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid came to investigate the growing threat within the ruined night elf temple. Overwhelmed and mortally weakened by the denizens within, he remains trapped and must rely on visiting adventurers to finish his duty and eliminate Kelris.",al={"argent guard thaelrid","why is thaelrid here","argent dawn in bfd"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous, ancient multi-headed hydra considered a primordial servant of the Old Gods. Slumbering beneath the sunken ruins, it awoke when deep subterranean corruption tainted the temple's sacred waters, and it now devours captives delivered by the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"akumai","who is akumai","aku'mai lore"},it="danger"},{q="Why turn the quest in to Bashana Runetotem?",a="Thaelrid directs Horde champions to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. As a steward of the Earthmother's balance, Bashana maintains communication with defenders against ancient evil and recognizes Kelris's Old God worship as an abhorrent blight upon Kalimdor.",al={"bashana runetotem","why thunder bluff","where to turn in blackfathom villainy"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Long ago, the subterranean complex was a sacred temple dedicated to the moon goddess Elune. Cataclysmic upheaval and ancient dark seepages from the earth tainted the grand Moon Well, allowing naga and doomsday cultists to claim the sunken sanctuaries for their dark master Aku'mai.",al={"history of blackfathom deeps","temple of elune ruins","why is bfd corrupted"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the goal of the Twilight's Hammer cult here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer seeks to revert the world to an age of primordial chaos by worshipping the Old Gods. Kelris seeks personal power through dark communion, feeding innocents into the depths to earn the favor of ancient entities.",al={"twilight's hammer motives","why cult in bfd","kelris goals"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Thaelrid want Twilight Lord Kelris slain?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris and his Twilight's Hammer cultists are actively sacrificing innocent captives to Aku'mai, a foul servant of the Old Gods, in exchange for dark power. Thaelrid was sent by the Argent Dawn to stop these horrors, and he cannot allow the cult's depravities and chaotic worship to continue unchecked.",al={"thaelrid motive","why does thaelrid want kelris dead","why kill kelris"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Thaelrid need your help instead of stopping Kelris himself?",a="Thaelrid has been cornered and imprisoned deep within the sunken temple. Weakened, drained, and completely out of strength, he cannot break out or face the cult leader on his own, leaving you as the only one capable of finishing his mission.",al={"why does thaelrid need help","why can't thaelrid fight kelris","thaelrid why me"},it="why_me",add=true},{q="What is the Head of Kelris for?",a="The head serves as undeniable proof of the cult leader's demise. Kelris had long evaded the Argent Dawn, leading many to believe he was already dead or lost, so presenting his head to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff confirms that his reign of terror and human sacrifice has truly ended.",al={"head of kelris purpose","what to do with head of kelris","why take kelris's head"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, entering into this pact with an Argent Dawn scout represents an uncommon moment of mutual interest against a cosmic blight, earning the early favor of the Dawn.",["race:Tauren"]="Bashana Runetotem sees the defeat of Kelris as a vital defense of the Earthmother, purging an abomination that sought to throw the world's natural order into primeval chaos.",["class:Druid"]="The defilement of an ancient night elf Moon Well by void-worshipping cultists and naga is an agonizing wound upon Kalimdor's natural and spiritual sanctuary.",["class:Shaman"]="The unrest stirred by Kelris and Aku'mai offends the balance of the elements, warping pure underground waters into a festering bed of shadow and sacrifice."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","bashana runetotem","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","kelris","moon well","thaelrid","twilight lord kelris","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","npc:bashana-runetotem","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Argent Guard Thaelrid",["end"]="Bashana Runetotem",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6561,ri={"Head of Kelris"}},src={"Blackfathom Villainy (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6562"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble in the Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="Trouble in the Deeps is a call for assistance sent from Stonetalon Mountains to the remote shores of Ashenvale. Tsunaman directs Horde adventurers to seek out the troll scholar Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, warning that dangerous forces lurk along the coast.",h="Trouble in the Deeps is a call for assistance sent from Stonetalon Mountains to the remote shores of...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Coast",b="In the arid crags of Stonetalon Mountains, Tsunaman recognizes that dark rumblings to the north demand attention. He charges capable Horde travelers with crossing into Ashenvale—the ancestral woodland of the night elves—to make contact with Je'neu Sancrea. Stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the far western edge known as the Zoram Strand, Je'neu has found himself confronted by mounting peril that requires outside intervention.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Zoram Strand",b="Reaching the western shore of Ashenvale is no trivial journey for Horde travelers. Whether cutting through the goblin-disturbed passes of Windshear Crag or moving north out of the Barrens, travelers must cross into hostile forest guarded fiercely by night elf sentinels. Far past the dense canopies, on the storm-washed coast of Zoram Strand, the lone outpost clings to survival while peering into the shadowed waters nearby.",sp=0},{t="Whispers Below the Waves",b="Upon arriving at the shore, Je'neu Sancrea reveals that the trouble brewing is rooted in the subterranean temple of Blackfathom Deeps. Ancient corruptions, foul water elementals, and Twilight's Hammer cultists have gathered beneath the tides, coaxing ancient evils back into the world. Je'neu relies on incoming champions to venture beneath the surface and confront the primordial terror stirred within the sunken halls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Trouble in the Deeps?",a="Tsunaman, located in the Stonetalon Mountains, offers the quest. He recognizes that allies along the Ashenvale coastline need reinforcements and points traveling Horde adventurers toward the sea.",al={"quest giver","who starts trouble in the deeps","tsunaman"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand, situated on the far western coastline of Ashenvale.",al={"where is je'neu","jeneu sancrea location","zoram'gar outpost"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you reach Zoram'gar Outpost from Stonetalon?",a="Travelers can journey northeast through Windshear Crag into Ashenvale, or loop east through the Barrens and enter the forest from the south. From central Ashenvale, head due west until reaching the open waters of the Zoram Strand.",al={"path to ashenvale","how to get to zoram strand","stonetalon to ashenvale route"},gp=true},{q="What trouble is Je'neu investigating?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is monitoring the nearby ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, where cultists and corrupt aquatic entities are stirring ancient horrors beneath the surface.",al={"what is happening at zoram strand","why does jeneu need help"},it="threat"},{q="What quest follows Trouble in the Deeps?",a="Speaking with Je'neu Sancrea leads directly into The Essence of Aku'Mai, which sends adventurers into Blackfathom Deeps to gather sapphire-hued elemental essence.",al={"next quest","trouble in the deeps follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the journey through Ashenvale considered perilous?",a="Ashenvale is the sovereign domain of the night elves, who fiercely resist any Horde encroachment. Travelers moving through the woodland risk running into hostile sentinels and elusive ambushers.",al={"ashenvale danger","night elf threat"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Tsunaman send you to Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Tsunaman knows that Je'neu Sancrea is isolated at the remote Zoram'gar Outpost and in desperate need of capable allies. Stationed on the far western coast of Ashenvale, Je'neu faces mounting dangers surrounding the mysterious depths of Blackfathom Deeps without sufficient support. Tsunaman dispatches you to reinforce him before hostile forces overwhelm the Horde's foothold.",al={"why does tsunaman want this done","why send me to ashenvale","tsunaman motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Holding ground at Zoram'gar Outpost is critical for securing the western flank of Kalimdor against both night elf forces and coastal horrors.",["class:Shaman"]="The disturbance beneath the waves of Zoram Strand threatens the balance of the local water spirits, demanding spiritual insight to cleanse the rot.",["race:Troll"]="Answering the call of Je'neu Sancrea provides Darkspear kin a vital chance to assist one of their foremost scholars in uncovering ancient Kalimdor mysteries."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","stonetalon mountains","tsunaman","windshear crag","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:tsunaman","npc:je-neu-sancrea","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","zone:blackfathom","quest:6563"},m={start="Tsunaman",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="22",faction="Horde",id=6562},src={"Trouble in the Deeps"}}
E["quest:6563"] = {t="quest",n="The Essence of Aku'Mai",z="blackfathom",s="Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost has noticed the naga of Blackfathom Deeps harvesting potent sapphire clusters from the caverns. Concerned by their magical properties and elemental water energies, the shaman tasks Horde adventurers with recovering the gems before they can be misused.",h="Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost has noticed the naga of Blackfathom Deeps harvesting potent sapphire...",sec={{t="A Threat in the Depths",b="On the mist-shrouded shores of the Zoram Strand, the Darkspear shaman Je'neu Sancrea keeps watch over ancient Kaldorei ruins now overrun by sinister forces. Deep within the submerged chambers of Blackfathom Deeps, naga have begun mining vibrant sapphire formations that sprout along the damp cavern walls. Sensing that the serpentine invaders seek to harness this volatile power, Sancrea seeks to intercept the harvest before their designs can come to fruition.",sp=0},{t="Water Spirits and Arcane Power",b="The Sapphires of Aku'mai are far more than ordinary gemstones; they thrum with elemental resonance and harbor clinging water spirits. In the hands of adept sorcerers, such conduits could fuel dangerous arcane rituals or amplify the influence of the shadowy hydra, Aku'mai, whose dark presence permeates the subterranean temple. Recovering these clusters deprives the naga of an invaluable reagent and safeguards the coastline from runaway elemental magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="The quest is offered by Je'neu Sancrea, a Darkspear troll shaman stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand in north-western Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who starts essence of akumai","jeneu sancrea location"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the naga want the Sapphires of Aku'Mai?",a="While their exact plot remains veiled, the sapphires possess potent elemental water energy and raw magical power, making them exceptionally dangerous reagents for naga spellcasting.",al={"why do naga want sapphires","what are the crystals for","sapphire purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the sapphire clusters found?",a="They line the cavern walls and floors in the outer tunnels and flooded passages of Blackfathom Deeps, just inside the ruined underground entrance along the Zoram Strand.",al={"where to find sapphires","sapphire of akumai location","crystal spawns"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous three-headed hydra dwelling deep within the submerged temple ruins. He is revered by the Twilight's Hammer cultists and feared as a favored pet of the Old Gods.",al={"who is akumai","what is akumai","aku'mai"},it="threat"},{q="Do I have to kill any dungeon bosses for this quest?",a="No. The sapphire clusters grow along the cavern walls in the earlier submerged tunnels before encountering the main bosses of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"do i need a full group","can i solo sapphires","boss requirement"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest connect to any other storyline?",a="Yes. It follows 'Trouble in the Deeps', forming part of Je'neu Sancrea's investigation into the rising darkness and cultist activity festering within Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"quest chain","prerequisites","trouble in the deeps"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the Sapphires of Aku'Mai?",a="Je'neu Sancrea noticed the naga systematically harvesting these crystal clusters from the cavern walls of Blackfathom Deeps. While their exact scheme remains unclear, he senses immense elemental energy lingering within the stones. He wants them collected before the naga can weaponize them as potent arcane components.",al={"jeneu sancrea motive","why gather sapphires","why collect sapphires of akumai"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Sapphire of Aku'Mai?",a="These sapphires are crystalline formations lining the submerged tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps. They resonate with raw elemental power, drawing water spirits to cling to them. Because of this natural concentration of energy, they serve as formidable arcane reagents if properly channeled.",al={"what are the sapphires","sapphire of akumai lore","sapphires of akumai power"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Je'neu Sancrea's reading of the crystals highlights the restless water spirits bound within them, a subtle warning that elemental forces are being corrupted beneath the temple.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's foothold at Zoram'gar Outpost is perilous; keeping the nearby naga from acquiring raw magical power helps protect the shoreline encampment.",["race:Troll"]="Je'neu Sancrea stands as an observant Darkspear mystic, relying on communion with the spirits and the wisdom of the ancestors to navigate the strange threats of Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","naga","sapphire of aku'mai","trouble in the deeps","water spirits","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:6562","zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-strand","npc:aku-mai","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",level="22",faction="Horde",id=6563,ri={"Sapphire of Aku'Mai"}},src={"The Essence of Aku'Mai (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6565"] = {t="quest",n="Allegiance to the Old Gods",z="blackfathom",s="Allegiance to the Old Gods is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with eliminating Lorgus Jett within the depths of Blackfathom Deeps. Directed by the Darkspear seer Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, the mission aims to disrupt the Twilight's Hammer cultists who seek to awaken ancient forces of destruction. Striking down Lorgus deals a direct blow to the cult's subversive operations beneath Ashenvale's coast.",h="Allegiance to the Old Gods is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with eliminating Lorgus Jett within the...",sec={{t="The Threat Beneath Zoram'gar",b="Perched on the strand of Ashenvale, the Horde outpost at Zoram'gar keeps a nervous watch over Blackfathom Deeps. The submerged temple complex has become a breeding ground for dark sorcery, overrun by naga, corrupted beasts, and the cloaked fanatics of the Twilight's Hammer. Je'neu Sancrea, an earthen ring seer stationed on the coast, recognizes that the cultists do not revere the natural balance or spirits of the land. Instead, they pledge their servitude to the Old Gods—monstrous beings of chaos defeated in ancient eras whose malign touch still lingers in Azeroth's forgotten places.",sp=0},{t="Ending Lorgus Jett",b="Je'neu tasks champions of the Horde with penetrating the subterranean ruins to hunt down Lorgus Jett, a crucial leader among the cultist ranks. Lorgus operates deep within the stone passageways spanning the chambers between the giant turtle Ghamoo-ra and the water elemental Baron Aquanis. Je'neu himself is too frail to march into the damp darkness, making the execution of Lorgus vital to severing whatever dark rituals the cultist sought to orchestrate beneath Ashenvale's waves.",sp=0},{t="Staving off Chaos",b="With the death of Lorgus Jett, the immediate ritualistic threat to the coast is contained, but Je'neu acknowledges that the Twilight's Hammer is far from eradicated. The cult's quiet infiltration of ancient holy sites signals a broader, creeping menace that seeks nothing less than the absolute return of the Old Gods. For the Horde at Zoram'gar, striking down Lorgus buys valuable time against an enemy that hides in the shadows of the world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lorgus Jett?",a="Lorgus Jett is a prominent leader among the Twilight's Hammer cultists established in Blackfathom Deeps. He directs cult rituals intended to usher in the return and reign of the ancient Old Gods.",al={"lorgus jett","who is lorgus","lorgus jett lore"},it="target"},{q="Where can Lorgus Jett be found in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lorgus Jett patrols the flooded corridors of Blackfathom Deeps, specifically in the connecting halls between the chamber of Ghamoo-ra and the altar area of Baron Aquanis.",al={"lorgus jett location","where is lorgus","find lorgus jett"},gp=true},{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll seer affiliated with the Earthen Ring, stationed at the Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale to monitor elemental disturbances and the corruption in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"je'neu sancrea","who gives allegiance to the old gods","jeneu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Je'neu care about the Twilight's Hammer?",a="As a seer dedicated to understanding nature and elemental balance, Je'neu views the Twilight's Hammer as an existential threat. The cult serves the Old Gods, chaotic ancient entities whose return would undo the harmony of the world.",al={"why fight twilight hammer","earthen ring old gods"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Old Gods?",a="The Old Gods are primordial beings of chaos and destruction that ruled Azeroth in the deep past before being defeated and buried away. The Twilight's Hammer cult actively worships them, scheming to break their seals and bring back their destructive rule.",al={"old gods lore","who are old gods","creatures of chaos"},it="threat"},{q="Why can't Je'neu Sancrea kill Lorgus Jett himself?",a="Je'neu admits to being too frail and weak to brave the hazards of Blackfathom Deeps on his own, relying on capable Horde champions to do the fighting while he tracks the spiritual and elemental disturbances from the outpost.",al={"why jeneu doesnt go","is jeneu weak"},it="why_me"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Taking down Lorgus Jett secures the periphery of Zoram'gar Outpost, protecting the Horde's isolated coastal encampment in Ashenvale from insidious cultist plots.",["class:Shaman"]="The Twilight's Hammer seeks to unleash elemental fury in service to chaotic Old Gods, making their eradication a priority for those sworn to maintain elemental balance alongside the Earthen Ring.",["race:Troll"]="Assisting Je'neu Sancrea honors the wisdom of a respected Darkspear seer working far from the Echo Isles to protect Azeroth's primal spirits."},kw={"allegiance to the old gods","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","lorgus jett","old gods","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar"},rel={"npc:lorgus-jett","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic","quest:6922","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6565},src={"Allegiance to the Old Gods (2)"}}
E["quest:6921"] = {t="quest",n="Amongst the Ruins",z="blackfathom",s="Tasked by Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Horde adventurers delve into the flooded temple of Blackfathom Deeps to recover a fathom core. The Earthen Ring seeks this relic to uncover the dark elemental plots of the invading Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="Tasked by Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Horde adventurers delve into the flooded temple of Blackfathom...",sec={{t="A Threat in the Deep",b="The ancient night elven temple of Blackfathom Deeps, once sacred to Elune, has fallen under the dominion of sinister forces. Deep within its submerged passages, the cultists of the Twilight's Hammer have established a stronghold. Stationed at the windswept shore of Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale, the Darkspear shaman Je'neu Sancrea observes the growing taint with rising alarm, recognizing that the cult intends to subjugate the local elements against the land and its defenders.",sp=0},{t="The Fathom Stone",b="To counter the cult's designs, Je'neu tasks Horde champions with securing a fathom core from the underwater fathom stone within the Moonshrine Ruins. When correctly deciphered by skilled shamans, the core reveals an exhaustive chronicle of elemental currents and disturbances. With this artifact in hand, the Earthen Ring hopes to pierce the veil of the Twilight's Hammer's operations and shield the region from elemental catastrophe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Amongst the Ruins?",a="The quest is provided by Je'neu Sancrea, a troll representative of the Earthen Ring stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost along the Zoram Strand in western Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts amongst the ruins"},it="identity"},{q="What is a fathom core?",a="A fathom core is a specialized artifact housed within a submerged fathom stone in the ruins. When read by shamans, it provides a comprehensive history of elemental activity, revealing how the local elements are being coerced and manipulated.",al={"what is the fathom core","fathom stone purpose","what does the core do"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Earthen Ring concerned about Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Earthen Ring seeks balance between the natural elements. The Twilight's Hammer cultists who have overtaken the submerged ruins are actively corrupting and coercing the elements to serve their dark ends, threatening the stability of the entire region.",al={"earthen ring motive","why does the earthen ring care","blackfathom deeps cultists"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the fathom stone located?",a="The fathom stone rests submerged in the waters of the Moonshrine Ruins inside Blackfathom Deeps, requiring explorers to dive beneath the surface to retrieve the core.",al={"where is the stone","fathom core location","moonshrine ruins fathom core"},gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players take this quest?",a="No. The quest is exclusive to the Horde, as Je'neu Sancrea operates out of the Horde outpost of Zoram'gar and aids the Horde's strategic presence in Ashenvale alongside his Earthen Ring duties.",al={"is this horde only","alliance version","can alliance do amongst the ruins"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What group is occupying Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The cavernous temple complex has been seized by the Twilight's Hammer, an apocalyptic cult dedicated to serving sinister Old God entities and twisting the elements toward catastrophic ends.",al={"who is in blackfathom","enemies in bfd","twilight's hammer blackfathom"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the Fathom Core recovered?",a="Je'neu Sancrea fears that the Twilight's Hammer cultists occupying Blackfathom Deeps will coerce the local elements into turning against the region and the Horde. Without the Fathom Core, the Earthen Ring is blind to what rituals and elemental disturbances the cult is conducting deep beneath the ruins.",al={"jeneu sancrea motive","why get the fathom core","why amongst the ruins"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Retrieving the fathom core directly serves the Earthen Ring's mission to protect the spirits of water and earth from being coerced by the Twilight's Hammer.",["faction:Horde"]="By clearing out threats within Blackfathom Deeps, you safeguard Zoram'gar Outpost and secure the Horde's contested foothold on the Ashenvale coast.",["race:Troll"]="Aiding Je'neu Sancrea helps a fellow Darkspear who bridges the divide between the Horde and the elemental caretakers of the Earthen Ring."},kw={"amongst the ruins","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6921,ri={"Fathom Core"}},src={"Amongst the Ruins (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6922"] = {t="quest",n="Baron Aquanis",z="blackfathom",s="Upon vanquishing the water elemental Baron Aquanis within Blackfathom Deeps, adventurers recover a Strange Water Globe containing tainted, putrid fluid. Brought to Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring, the artifact provides crucial evidence of the elemental corruption spreading beneath Ashenvale. Je'neu believes it will prove what corrupted the baron, and he wouldn't be surprised if it were the Twilight's Hammer cultists lurking in the submerged ruins.",h="Upon vanquishing the water elemental Baron Aquanis within Blackfathom Deeps, adventurers recover a Strange...",sec={{t="A Corrupted Heart",b="Baron Aquanis was no ordinary water spirit, but a powerful elemental corrupted by foul sorcery within the flooded grottos of Blackfathom Deeps. When destroyed, the elemental leaves behind a Strange Water Globe—an impervious orb holding a sloshing, putrid fluid that seemingly sustained and warped the creature's natural essence. The object defies physical damage, harboring energies that are deeply distressing to those attuned to the balance of the elements.",sp=0},{t="Studies of the Earthen Ring",b="Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman stationed on the Zoram Strand, recognizes the artifact immediately as evidence of unnatural meddling. He and his order have long suspected that Baron Aquanis had fallen prey to dark forces, pointing the finger directly at the Twilight's Hammer cultists who occupy the sunken temple. By studying the globe, Je'neu hopes not only to verify the cult's culpability, but to discover the exact dark methods they use to subjugate and twist Azeroth's elemental spirits.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental inhabiting the subterranean waters of Blackfathom Deeps. Rather than roaming freely, Aquanis has been corrupted and bound by the dark practitioners who dwell within the ruined temple complex.",al={"who is aquanis","aquanis boss","baron aquanis lore"},it="target"},{q="What is the Strange Water Globe?",a="The Strange Water Globe is an impervious sphere left behind after defeating Baron Aquanis. Inside, a foul, putrid liquid sloshes around, serving as the source of tainted energy that fueled the elemental's corrupted state.",al={"water globe","strange water globe","aquanis quest item"},it="item"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the globe?",a="As a member of the Earthen Ring, Je'neu Sancrea monitors elemental disturbances across Ashenvale. He studies the globe to confirm whether the Twilight's Hammer is behind the corruption and to unravel the rituals used to twist the spirits.",al={"why bring to jeneu","jeneu sancrea purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is behind the corruption of Baron Aquanis?",a="The primary suspects are the Twilight's Hammer cultists nesting deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. Their presence in the temple aligns with a campaign of desecration and dark communion with unnatural beings.",al={"who corrupted aquanis","aquanis twilight hammer","cultists blackfathom"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is an Earthen Ring shaman encamped along the Zoram Strand on the northwestern coast of Ashenvale, near the entrance to the Blackfathom Deeps cavern system.",al={"where is jeneu","turn in aquanis quest","where to turn in water globe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What follows the turn-in of this quest?",a="Handing over the globe leads directly to further investigations into the elemental distress of the region, prompting adventurers to continue aiding the Earthen Ring against the growing blight.",al={"next quest","elemental distress"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Earthen Ring takes the corruption of elemental spirits as a grave violation of the natural order. Investigating Baron Aquanis's tainted state is central to restoring elemental balance.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu Sancrea coordinates with Horde scouts at the Zoram'gar Outpost, seeking courageous champions to cleanse the corrupted waters lurking beneath Ashenvale's coast."},kw={"ashenvale","baron aquanis","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","elemental corruption","je'neu sancrea","strange water globe","twilight's hammer","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},m={start="Strange Water Globe",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6922},src={"Baron Aquanis (quest)"}}
E["quest:824"] = {t="quest",n="Je'neu of the Earthen Ring",z="blackfathom",s="This errand directs Horde adventurers to deliver a corrupted water globe recovered from Ashenvale's elementals to Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring. As a shaman dedicated to elemental harmony, Je'neu seeks to understand the spreading corruption along the Zoram Strand and within Blackfathom Deeps. Studying the relic offers hope of halting the unnatural blight poisoning the region's waters.",h="This errand directs Horde adventurers to deliver a corrupted water globe recovered from Ashenvale's...",sec={{t="A Messenger for the Elements",b="When strange, contaminated elementals began surfacing across Ashenvale, scouts took notice of the unnatural power animating them. Among the remains lay a befouled water globe, an intact vessel pulsing with corrupted magic. Knowing standard soldiers and scouts lacked the spiritual insight to diagnose such an anomaly, Mastok Wrilehiss directed Horde travelers to seek out someone with deep knowledge of ancient legends and elemental lore: Je'neu Sancrea.",sp=0},{t="The Eyes of the Earthen Ring",b="Je'neu Sancrea belongs to the Earthen Ring, an order of shamans committed to preserving balance among the primal forces of Azeroth. While Horde forces guard the frontier along the Zoram Strand, Je'neu concentrates on the spiritual wound festering in the nearby temple ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. To him, an elemental drawing power from a tainted vessel is not merely an isolated threat, but an alarming omen that unseen, ancient powers are perverting the natural order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a troll shaman representing the Earthen Ring in northern Kalimdor. He devotes his life to communing with and studying the elements, stationing himself near the Zoram Strand to investigate dark disturbances rising from Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who is jeneu","jeneu sancrea lore","what is jeneu doing here"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an organization of shamans dedicated to keeping Azeroth's primal elements in harmony. They delve into ancient lore, forgotten spirits, and old legends to mend elemental chaos and heal spiritual corruption across the world.",al={"what is earthen ring","who are earthen ring","earthen ring lore"},it="people"},{q="Where can Je'neu Sancrea be found?",a="Je'neu can be found at Zoram'gar Outpost on the coast of the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, where he studies the elemental disturbances rising from nearby Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is jeneu","jeneu location","find jeneu sancrea"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Befouled Water Globe?",a="The globe is a magical conduit through which powerful water elementals channel their strength. Finding one corrupted and intact suggests dark forces in the area are deliberately twisting and enslaving the local spirits.",al={"what is the globe","befouled globe lore","water globe"},it="item"},{q="Who sends you to speak with Je'neu?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss, a Horde officer stationed in Ashenvale, directs adventurers to deliver the tainted relic to Je'neu after realizing the army cannot decipher its strange magical nature.",al={"who starts this quest","mastok quest"},it="origin"},{q="What will Je'neu do with the globe?",a="Je'neu takes custody of the vessel so the Earthen Ring can examine the nature of its blight, hoping the research will reveal a way to cleanse the waters and restore peace to the region's troubled elementals.",al={"what happens to the globe","cure the corruption"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mastok Wrilehiss send you to Je'neu?",a="Mastok recognizes that the Befouled Water Globe is far beyond his expertise. Understanding corrupt magic, old legends, and disturbed elementals falls squarely into the realm of the Earthen Ring. He sends you to Je'neu Sancrea because Je'neu is a local shaman of the Ring who possesses the deep elemental knowledge needed to unravel the globe's true significance and threat.",al={"mastok wrilehiss motive","why send to jeneu","why does mastok want this done"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This task directly touches the shamanistic duty of maintaining elemental balance. Delivering the corrupted globe aids a fellow member of the Earthen Ring in diagnosing a dangerous spiritual sickness.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde establishes fortified camps like Zoram'gar Outpost in Ashenvale, unearthing the dark origins behind local elemental hostility is vital for securing the coastline.",["race:Troll"]="Je'neu Sancrea demonstrates the deep spiritual wisdom of the Darkspear, applying his ancestral bond with the spirits on behalf of the Earthen Ring."},kw={"befouled water globe","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","elementals","je'neu sancrea","mastok wrilehiss","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:1918","npc:mastok-wrilehiss","subzone:zoram-strand","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","topic:old-god"},m={start="Mastok Wrilehiss",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",faction="Horde",id=824},src={"Je'neu of the Earthen Ring (quest)"}}
E["quest:971"] = {t="quest",n="Knowledge in the Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="Knowledge in the Deeps is an Alliance quest offered by Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern. He tasks adventurers with trekking across the sea to the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale to recover the ancient Lorgalis Manuscript. Beneath Bonegrip's scholar veneer lies an ominous agenda tied to dark entities and apocalyptic prophecy.",h="Knowledge in the Deeps is an Alliance quest offered by Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern.",sec={{t="A Scholar in the Shadows",b="Hidden away in the damp reaches of Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, Gerrig Bonegrip presents himself as a devoted collector of ancient texts. Yet his scholarly pursuits carry a distinctly sinister undertone. Bonegrip is not interested in mundane history or civic chronicles; he explicitly hunts for forgotten lore capable of opening doorways and awakening 'Those Who Sleep.' His talk of surviving beyond 'the end days' marks him as an eccentric—or a dangerous devotee of shadowy, slumbering powers.",sp=0},{t="The Sunken Ruin of Lorgalis",b="Bonegrip directs seekers halfway across Azeroth to the shadowed shores of Ashenvale, where the ancient night elven sanctuary of Blackfathom Deeps lies drowned. Before the Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart, night elven scholars gathered immense magical knowledge in their coastal temples. Amidst the flooded corridors, now crawling with naga, satyrs, and Twilight's Hammer cultists, rests the Lorgalis Manuscript—a text of forbidden lore kept in a Pitted Iron Chest.",sp=0},{t="Brothers and Sisters",b="When presented with the watersoaked manuscript, Bonegrip makes no effort to file it in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. Instead, he openly rejoices that duplicates will be produced and disseminated among his mysterious 'brothers and sisters.' While grateful to the Alliance adventurer who retrieved it, Bonegrip's loyalties clearly lie with a clandestine sect eager to utilize the recovered lore for esoteric, world-altering rites. Bonegrip is associated with the Twilight's Hammer, whose followers seek forbidden knowledge of the Old Gods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Knowledge in the Deeps?",a="The quest is given by Gerrig Bonegrip, a dwarven lore-seeker found residing in the dimly lit Forlorn Cavern within the dwarven mountain city of Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts knowledge in the deeps"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="The Lorgalis Manuscript is a text Gerrig Bonegrip wants recovered from Blackfathom Deeps. It is kept in a Pitted Iron Chest among the flooded ruins.",al={"what is lorgalis manuscript","lorgalis lore","what book do i find"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Lorgalis Manuscript located?",a="The manuscript rests deep inside the Blackfathom Deeps dungeon, located along the Zoram Strand on the northwestern coast of Ashenvale in Kalimdor.",al={"lorgalis manuscript location","where is the book in bfd","bfd book location"},gp=true},{q="Who are 'Those Who Sleep' mentioned by Gerrig Bonegrip?",a="Bonegrip uses this cryptic name for the slumbering powers described in the forbidden lore he collects. The quest's protected sections explore his darker connections.",al={"those who sleep","who is bonegrip talking about","what does gerrig worship"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the 'brothers and sisters' Gerrig plans to share the manuscript with?",a="Bonegrip's associates share his interest in forbidden lore. Recovering the manuscript can reveal more about whom he serves.",al={"gerrig brothers and sisters","who is gerrig working for","bonegrip faction"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Why does a quest in Ironforge send players all the way to Ashenvale?",a="Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern attracts unsanctioned magic users, warlocks, and rogues seeking secrets hidden from the light. Bonegrip collects old, powerful lore, and the Lorgalis Manuscript he wants is rumored to lie at the bottom of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale, the old dwelling of long-dead elves who held great knowledge.",al={"why go to ashenvale","ironforge to bfd quest","travel to blackfathom"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gerrig Bonegrip want the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip collects ancient, powerful texts capable of opening forgotten doorways and awakening Those Who Sleep. He believes the Lorgalis Manuscript holds long-lost secrets from the ancient night elves of Blackfathom Deeps, and he intends to copy and distribute its dark knowledge among his secretive brothers and sisters before the coming end days.",al={"gerrig bonegrip motive","why does gerrig want the manuscript","gerrig bonegrip quest reason"},sp=1,it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Bonegrip operates right alongside the warlocks hiding in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, sharing their hunger for forbidden, planar-bending texts.",["race:NightElf"]="The manuscript lies in Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned night elven sanctuary now occupied by cultists and other intruders.",["faction:Alliance"]="While helping an Alliance scholar appears harmless, Bonegrip's true motives and shadowy associates hint at darker designs operating within Ironforge's walls."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","ironforge","knowledge in the deeps","lorgalis manuscript"},rel={"npc:gerrig-bonegrip","zone:blackfathom","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ironforge","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=971,ri={"Lorgalis Manuscript"}},src={"Knowledge in the Deeps (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:aku-mai-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Aku'mai's Lair",z="blackfathom",s="Aku'mai's Lair is the deepest and darkest cavern within Blackfathom Deeps. Located beyond the Moonshrine Sanctum, this submerged hollow serves as the nesting ground for Aku'mai, a monstrous hydra venerated as a harbinger of the Old Gods.",h="Aku'mai's Lair is the deepest and darkest cavern within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Heart of the Depths",b="Sealed away behind the Moonshrine Sanctum, Aku'mai's Lair represents the culmination of the corruption sweeping Blackfathom Deeps. To enter the cavern, dark rituals must be engaged by igniting the four brazier fires flanking a naga statue, awakening guardians sworn to defend the threshold. Beyond these heavy double doors lies a sunless, flooded grotto. Here, both the Twilight's Hammer cultists and invading naga gather in reverence of Aku'mai, an ancient three-headed hydra considered a primordial devourer and living servant of the Old Gods.",sp=0},{t="Harbinger of Ruin",b="The presence of Aku'mai within the lair makes it a focal point for the apocalyptic plans of the Twilight's Hammer. The cultists revere the great beast as an omen of a promised age of darkness, believing its emergence and continued sustenance will herald the breaking of subterranean prisons holding their ancient deities. Fed by sacrificial offerings and guarded zealously by dark magic, the subterranean pool serves as a grim symbol of the ancient evil clawing its way back into Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Aku'mai's Lair located?",a="Aku'mai's Lair is found at the very end of the Blackfathom Deeps cavern complex in Ashenvale, situated just beyond the sealed doors of the Moonshrine Sanctum.",al={"where is akumai lair","how to get to akumai room","akumai lair location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you open the doors to Aku'mai's Lair?",a="The double doors leading into the lair are unlocked by lighting the four ritual braziers surrounding the naga statue within the Moonshrine Sanctum and defeating the waves of creatures summoned to protect them.",al={"open akumai door","how to unlock akumai lair","light fires akumai"},gp=true},{q="What dwells inside this cavern?",a="The cavern is inhabited by Aku'mai, a massive three-headed hydra tainted by ancient dark powers, serving as a pet and manifestation of the Old Gods' will.",al={"who is in akumai lair","what lives in akumai lair","boss in akumai lair"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult worshiping here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer venerates Aku'mai as an apocalyptic herald whose rise foreshadows the freeing of their dark masters from their underground prisons to destroy the world.",al={"why do cultists worship akumai","twilights hammer akumai lair","why is twilight hammer here"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Aku'mai's Lair?",a="Aku'mai's Lair is the deepest, darkest cavern within the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Once part of an ancient night elven temple dedicated to Elune, this flooded hollow now serves as the sanctum for a monstrous three-headed hydra, a creature steeped in the malevolent influence of the Old Gods.",al={"what is akumais lair","akumai lair info","about akumais lair"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to turn this place into Aku'mai's Lair?",a="Following the ancient Great Sundering, the temple of Blackfathom sank beneath the tides and fell into forgotten ruin. Over the centuries, corruption seeped into its flooded underbelly, allowing the dread hydra Aku'mai to claim these submerged chambers as a nest while dark cultists and naga gathered to venerate it.",al={"akumais lair history","what happened at akumais lair","how did akumais lair form"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Aku'mai's Lair dangerous?",a="It is extraordinarily perilous. Beyond the gauntlet of zealots and naga guarding the Moonshrine Sanctum, the lair itself houses a colossal servant of the Old Gods. Aku'mai lashes out with caustic breath, crushing fury, and primordial malice capable of tearing apart unprepared adventurers.",al={"is akumais lair dangerous","how dangerous is akumais lair","danger akumais lair"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is this cavern called Aku'mai's Lair?",a="The cavern takes its name from its monstrous inhabitant, Aku'mai. The massive, corrupted hydra has dwelt here long enough to claim the hollow as its personal nesting ground, revered by the Twilight's Hammer and naga who wait upon its dark awakening.",al={"why is it called akumais lair","akumais lair name meaning","who named akumais lair"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For the night elves, seeing a desecrated Elune temple culminating in a filthy nest for a foul Old God spawn is an intolerable defilement of sacred Ashenvale soil.",["class:Druid"]="The vile mutation and unnatural corruption radiating from Aku'mai's watery den represents a severe blight on the natural waterways and beasts of Kalimdor."},kw={"aku'mai's lair","akumai","blackfathom deeps","hydra","moonshrine sanctum","naga","old gods","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:aku-mai","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:naga"},src={"Aku'mai's Lair"}}
E["subzone:drowned-sacellum"] = {t="subzone",n="Drowned Sacellum",z="blackfathom",s="The Drowned Sacellum is a submerged elven shrine lying just inside the entrance of Blackfathom Deeps. Submerged beneath brackish saltwater and draped in cavernous roots, its shattered masonry is now overrun by murlocs and makrura.",h="The Drowned Sacellum is a submerged elven shrine lying just inside the entrance of Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Submerged Sanctuary",b="Stepping through the threshold of Blackfathom Deeps immediately brings explorers into the Drowned Sacellum. Once a tranquil subterranean chapel dedicated to Elune, the sacellum has long collapsed into the sea-swept abyss beneath Ashenvale's coast. Saltwater pools swallow ancient marble flagstones overgrown with starfish, while massive tree roots dangle from the cavern ceiling above. Dark, flickering wisps provide the only dim light in the gloom, illuminating a ruined pathway of stones that adventurers must carefully navigate to reach the Pool of Ask'ar deeper within the temple complex.",sp=0},{t="Den of Scavengers",b="Long abandoned by its night elf caretakers, the Drowned Sacellum has fallen into the hands of shoreline scavengers. Packs of aggressive murlocs and heavily armored makrura dwell side by side in the murky waters, attacking anyone who dares disturb their nesting grounds. While darker, cultic threats lurk further below in the temple depths, these predatory creatures form the first hazardous line of defense for the subterranean ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Drowned Sacellum originally used for?",a="A sacellum is a small roofless shrine or chapel. In ancient times before the Sundering, it served as an elven place of worship within the greater subterranean temple complex dedicated to the moon goddess Elune.",al={"drowned sacellum purpose","what is the drowned sacellum","sacellum history"},it="purpose"},{q="What creatures inhabit this part of the caverns?",a="The flooded ruins are occupied primarily by wild murlocs and makrura. They thrive in the brackish saltwater pools and nesting crevices of the cavern.",al={"drowned sacellum mobs","what lives in drowned sacellum","monsters in drowned sacellum"},it="residents"},{q="How do you navigate past the Drowned Sacellum?",a="Travelers must carefully leap across the crumbling, half-submerged platforms and pillars rising out of the water to access the tunnel leading forward to the Pool of Ask'ar.",al={"how to get through drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum jump","path to pool of askar"},gp=true},{q="Where does the light in the cavern come from?",a="Faint, eerie illumination filters down from dark wisps floating among the thick, twisted tree roots that pierce through the ceiling from the Ashenvale forests above.",al={"why is it glowing","wisps in drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum lighting"}},{q="What is the Drowned Sacellum?",a="The Drowned Sacellum is a ruined, subterranean shrine located just inside the entrance of the Blackfathom Deeps caverns. Lying half-submerged in a pool of dark saltwater, its ancient stonework is now crusted over with starfish and choked by the thick tree roots hanging from the cavern ceiling above.",al={"what is drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum lore","drowned sacellum blackfathom"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Drowned Sacellum?",a="A sacellum is a small, consecrated shrine or chapel. This particular sanctuary earned its grim moniker because the surrounding ocean waters have seeped into the subterranean caverns, completely flooding its chambers and leaving its sacred altar partially submerged under saltwater.",al={"why drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum name meaning","sacellum name origin"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Drowned Sacellum dangerous?",a="Yes. Though it was once a sacred place of worship, the drowned shrine is now infested by aggressive murlocs and armored makrura. They dwell together among the murky pools and ruined pillars, viciously attacking anyone attempting to delve deeper into the Blackfathom caverns.",al={"is drowned sacellum safe","drowned sacellum threats","danger drowned sacellum"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing an ancient, sacred shrine submerged in saltwater and fouled by murlocs is a bitter reminder of the sacred Kaldorei heritage lost beneath the Zoram Strand.",["class:Druid"]="Massive tree roots continue to breach the stone ceiling from the surface above, proof that nature endures even amidst corrupted underground waters."},kw={"bfd","blackfathom deeps","drowned sacellum","makrura","murloc","shrine","zoram strand"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:murloc","npc:umpi"},src={"Drowned Sacellum"}}
E["subzone:forgotten-pool"] = {t="subzone",n="Forgotten Pool",z="blackfathom",s="The Forgotten Pool is a submerged cavern tucked deep beneath the flooded corridors of Blackfathom Deeps. Located beyond the Moonshrine Ruins, this quiet dead-end serves as the aquatic lair of monstrous deep-sea predators lurking in the subterranean dark.",h="The Forgotten Pool is a submerged cavern tucked deep beneath the flooded corridors of Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Submerged Lair",b="Reaching the Forgotten Pool requires diving into the sunken subterranean waterways extending past the Moonshrine Ruins. Cut off from dry ground, the pool is an isolated, stagnant cavern completely flooded by dark waters. Away from the chanting Twilight's Hammer cultists and the patrolling naga, this secluded pocket serves as the lair of the ancient aquatic terror known as Old Serra'kis, keeping the beast hidden in the flooded dark.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forgotten Pool located?",a="The Forgotten Pool is an entirely submerged underwater cavern situated deep within Blackfathom Deeps. To reach it, explorers must swim through the flooded tunnels branching off past the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"where is forgotten pool","forgotten pool location","how to find forgotten pool"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What lurks inside the Forgotten Pool?",a="The cavern serves as the hidden lair of Old Serra'kis, an ancient thresher-like beast of the deep waters that makes the secluded dead-end its lair.",al={"forgotten pool monster","who lives in forgotten pool","forgotten pool boss"},it="threat"},{q="Does the Forgotten Pool lead anywhere else?",a="No. The pool is an underwater dead-end with no further passageways, serving strictly as a secluded aquatic nest.",al={"is forgotten pool a dead end","where does forgotten pool go"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Forgotten Pool?",a="The Forgotten Pool is a flooded subterranean cavern tucked away in the depths of Blackfathom Deeps, just beyond the Moonshrine Ruins. Cut off from the temple corridors by submerged passages, it forms a stagnant, secluded aquatic dead-end deep beneath the ruins of the ancient night elven sanctuary.",al={"what is forgotten pool","forgotten pool lore","about forgotten pool"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Forgotten Pool dangerous?",a="Yes, swimming through its dark, waterlogged tunnels presents severe perils. Beyond the risk of drowning in the submerged passages, the pool serves as the lair of Old Serra'kis, a monstrous aquatic thresher, alongside other lurking horrors that make diving into its depths perilous for any unwary explorer.",al={"is forgotten pool dangerous","danger forgotten pool","forgotten pool threats"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde scouts venturing into Blackfathom Deeps may find Old Serra'kis lurking in the flooded dark of the pool, far from the cult's chanting halls."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","cavern","forgotten pool","moonshrine ruins","old serra'kis","thresher","underwater"},rel={"npc:old-serra-kis","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"Forgotten Pool"}}
E["subzone:moonshrine-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonshrine Ruins",z="blackfathom",s="The Moonshrine Ruins are a flooded expanse of ancient night elven architecture deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Once dedicated to the worship of Elune, these crumbling halls have been desecrated and seized by the Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="The Moonshrine Ruins are a flooded expanse of ancient night elven architecture deep within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Flooded Halls of Elune",b="Past the cavernous Pool of Ask'ar lies the Moonshrine Ruins, a somber testament to the night elves' ancient past along the Ashenvale coast. These partially submerged halls once rang with chants honoring the Moon Goddess Elune, but the Great Sundering shattered the temple and drowned its lower levels in sea water. Today, the murky waters churn with feral aquatic beasts, from aggressive crabs to serpentine threshadons, while the Twilight's Hammer cult maintains an active presence throughout the stones, bent on dark rituals that mock the shrine's sacred origin.",sp=0},{t="The Elemental Depths",b="Connecting directly toward the Forgotten Pool and the Moonshrine Sanctum, the ruins serve as a staging ground for the cult's summonings. Beneath the surface of the flooded chambers sits an ancient runestone bound to the elements. Through this aquatic focus, the Twilight's Hammer manipulates the waters of the deeps, calling forth Baron Aquanis, a monstrous water elemental bound to their dark designs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What were the Moonshrine Ruins originally built for?",a="The ruins were originally part of a grand underground temple complex dedicated to the night elven goddess Elune, constructed before the Great Sundering tore the ancient continent apart.",al={"moonshrine origins","who built moonshrine ruins","what is this place"},it="origin"},{q="Who controls the Moonshrine Ruins now?",a="The ruins are infested with hostile aquatic beasts like threshadons and snapping crabs, alongside cultists belonging to the Twilight's Hammer, who have overrun the entire sunken complex.",al={"who is here","moonshrine mobs","twilights hammer blackfathom"},it="residents"},{q="Where do the Moonshrine Ruins lead?",a="The ruins lie past the tunnels beyond the Pool of Ask'ar. From the Moonshrine Ruins, pathways connect directly deeper toward the Moonshrine Sanctum and provide access to the Forgotten Pool.",al={"moonshrine exits","where does this go","path through ruins"},it="place"},{q="Who is Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental summoned by touching a submerged runestone hidden in the murky water beneath the ruins, serving the sinister aims of the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"baron aquanis lore","underwater boss moonshrine","elemental in water"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Moonshrine Ruins?",a="The Moonshrine Ruins are a sunken cavern complex situated deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Once an ancient night elven sanctuary dedicated to Elune, the halls are now partially submerged beneath subterranean waters. Corrupted cultists and feral aquatic predators prowl through the ruined arches and flooded chambers.",al={"what is moonshrine ruins","moonshrine ruins lore","about moonshrine ruins"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is the Moonshrine Ruins so dangerous?",a="The ruins harbor both fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists and vicious aquatic wildlife. Swarming crabs and massive threshadons churn through the flooded pathways, ready to drag swimmers down, while cultists conduct dark rituals in the shadows.",al={"is moonshrine ruins dangerous","moonshrine ruins danger","threats in moonshrine ruins"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Moonshrine Ruins?",a="The chamber draws its name from the ancient night elven shrines that originally honored the moon goddess, Elune. Following the Sundering and centuries of neglect, those once-glorious holy places collapsed into the flooded, broken stones you see today.",al={"why is it called moonshrine ruins","moonshrine ruins name","moonshrine meaning"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing these sacred halls dedicated to Elune reduced to flooded, cult-infested ruins is a bitter grievance for any night elf journeying into the deeps.",["class:Shaman"]="The binding of water spirits like Baron Aquanis via dark runestones reveals how deeply the Twilight's Hammer distorts and enslaves elemental forces."},kw={"aquanis","blackfathom","moonshrine","ruins","sanctum","threshadon","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","quest:6922","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","subzone:forgotten-pool","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Moonshrine Ruins"}}
E["subzone:moonshrine-sanctum"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonshrine Sanctum",z="blackfathom",s="Moonshrine Sanctum is an ancient elven shrine deep within Blackfathom Deeps, now serving as the inner redoubt for the Twilight's Hammer cult. Presided over by Twilight Lord Kelris, the chamber houses a pristine monument to Queen Azshara and directly guards the sealed entrance to Aku'mai's lair.",h="Moonshrine Sanctum is an ancient elven shrine deep within Blackfathom Deeps, now serving as the inner redoubt...",sec={{t="A Desecrated Temple",b="Situated just beyond the flooded Moonshrine Ruins, the Moonshrine Sanctum represents the central hub of cultist activity inside Blackfathom Deeps. Though originally built millennia ago by night elves to honor the moon and their rulers, the hall is now defiled by the Twilight's Hammer. Interestingly, the cultists have carefully maintained the towering effigy of Queen Azshara, finding kinship with the serpentine naga who serve the same dark, submerged masters. Under the watchful gaze of Twilight Lord Kelris, dark rituals are chanted day and night beneath the cavernous stone ceiling.",sp=0},{t="The Threshold to Aku'mai",b="The sanctum acts as the final barricade before Aku'mai's Lair. Heavy double stone doors seal away the monstrous hydra, held fast by ancient warding enchantments. Surrounding Azshara's central statue are four ritual braziers that must be ignited to unravel the seal. Doing so disturbs the slumbering guardians of the shrine—hordes of giant crabs, snapped-jaw turtles, armored makrura, and conjured water elementals bound to defend the sanctum against unwary intruders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="The Moonshrine Sanctum is located deep inside the Blackfathom Deeps dungeon along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. It lies just past the flooded Moonshrine Ruins, immediately preceding the lair of the hydra Aku'mai.",al={"moonshrine sanctum location","where is moonshrine sanctum","bfd sanctum"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who rules over the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris commands the sanctum. He is a formidable sleep-weaving sorcerer of the Twilight's Hammer cult who conducts rituals to honor their ancient void-touched patron.",al={"who leads here","boss of moonshrine sanctum","who runs the sanctum"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is there an intact statue of Azshara here?",a="The sanctum was originally an ancient elven temple dedicated to Queen Azshara prior to the Great Sundering. The Twilight's Hammer maintains the effigy in pristine shape because the cult works in direct league with Azshara's naga beneath the deeps.",al={"azshara statue","why statue of azshara","naga statue bfd"},it="origin"},{q="How do you open the large doors at the back of the chamber?",a="To unlock the doors leading into Aku'mai's Lair, adventurers must ignite four ritual candles set around the feet of the Azshara statue. Lighting each candle awakens waves of guardian aquatic beasts and water elementals that must be subdued.",al={"how to open bfd doors","akumai door open","light candles bfd"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="The Moonshrine Sanctum is an ancient temple chamber deep within the Blackfathom Deeps. Once devoted to Queen Azshara, it now serves as the inner seat of power for the local Twilight's Hammer cult, who conduct dark rituals in the presence of an intact monument to the naga queen.",al={"what is moonshrine sanctum","moonshrine sanctum info","about moonshrine sanctum"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="Originally built as an ancient elven shrine dedicated to Queen Azshara, the sanctum survived the Great Sundering beneath the waters of Ashenvale. In recent times, the Twilight's Hammer cult discovered the subterranean temple and claimed it as their high seat, repurposing its ancient halls to perform dark rites.",al={"moonshrine sanctum history","what happened at moonshrine sanctum","history of moonshrine sanctum"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Moonshrine Sanctum dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The chamber is heavily guarded by fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists led by Twilight Lord Kelris. Furthermore, the shrine itself is warded by dangerous guardians, and it lies right before the threshold to Aku'mai's lair.",al={"how dangerous is moonshrine sanctum","is moonshrine sanctum safe","dangers of moonshrine sanctum"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Seeing an ancient temple carved by your ancestors in the age before the Sundering perverted into a sacrificial hollow for the Twilight's Hammer and naga is a sickening testament to Ashenvale's encroaching shadows.",["class:Priest"]="The twisted rituals performed by Twilight Lord Kelris in this chamber invert sacred devotions, channeling maddening whispers of the void rather than restorative divine prayer."},kw={"aku'mai","azshara","blackfathom","candles","kelris","moonshrine","sanctum","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","subzone:aku-mai-s-lair","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga"},src={"Moonshrine Sanctum"}}
E["subzone:pool-of-ask-ar"] = {t="subzone",n="Pool of Ask'ar",z="blackfathom",s="The Pool of Ask'ar is a sprawling, submerged cavern lake located deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Teeming with aquatic beasts and foul naga invaders, its waters conceal ancient night elven architecture alongside hidden passageways that wind deeper into the corrupted sanctuary.",h="The Pool of Ask'ar is a sprawling, submerged cavern lake located deep within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Depths of the Sunken Grotto",b="Situated just beyond the Drowned Sacellum, the Pool of Ask'ar fills a massive subterranean vault with murky, cold water. The natural caverns and ancient stonework have become a nesting ground for oversized snapping turtles and deep-sea crabs, overseen by the enormous ancient chelonian known as Ghamoo-ra. The naga who have taken over the temple utilize this submerged threshold as a defensive staging ground, guarding the waterlogged approaches that lead deeper into the complex toward Lady Sarevess and the Moonshrine Ruins.",sp=0},{t="Secrets Beneath the Surface",b="Beyond its monstrous fauna and hostile patrols, the waters of the pool hide valuable relics from the shrine's pre-Sundering past. Submerged ledges and hidden alcoves along the cavern's edges conceal lost artifacts, including the valuable Lorgalis Manuscript sought by the dwarven scholar Gerrig Bonegrip of Ironforge. Swimming through the flooded southern passageways brings travelers out into dry tunnels guarded by vile murlocs and Old God cultists, marking the pool as the critical aquatic crossroads of Blackfathom Deeps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?",a="It is a vast subterranean pool within Blackfathom Deeps, located right past the Drowned Sacellum. It is dominated by snapping turtles, crabs, and naga guards.",al={"pool of askar","what is this pool","bfd water area"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in this subterranean pool?",a="The cavern is inhabited by wild reef creatures such as snapping turtles and crabs, most notably the colossal turtle Ghamoo-ra. Hostile naga also patrol the submerged banks and nearby chambers.",al={"pool monsters","pool of askar bosses","who is in the pool"},it="residents"},{q="Where do the underwater tunnels lead?",a="Navigating the flooded southern passages leads out toward chambers occupied by Lady Sarevess and Argent Guard Thaelrid, and opens into the path winding past Gelihast toward the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"pool tunnels","where does the water go","pool of askar exit"},gp=true},{q="What notable items can be found in the pool?",a="The submerged ruins along the pool's periphery contain the Lorgalis Manuscript, an ancient text on the Old Gods coveted by Gerrig Bonegrip of Ironforge.",al={"pool of askar relics","lorgalis manuscript","pool loot"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is the Pool of Ask'ar dangerous?",a="Venturing into this flooded cavern poses severe danger. Hostile naga patrol the surrounding ruins and passages, while aggressive subterranean crabs and snapjaws infest the dark waters. Even deeper beneath the surface, ancient and colossal beasts lurk, ready to drag unwary swimmers into the suffocating depths.",al={"is pool of ask'ar dangerous","pool of askar danger","threats in pool of askar"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The pool floods what was once holy Elune temple grounds, drowning ancient architecture and scattering sacred relics like the Lorgalis Manuscript to be scavenged by naga.",["faction:Alliance"]="The waterways must be breached to uncover the fate of Argent Guard Thaelrid, who ventured into these cavern depths on a holy mission against the Twilight's Hammer."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","drowned sacellum","ghamoo-ra","lady sarevess","lorgalis manuscript","naga","pool of ask'ar"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic","subzone:drowned-sacellum","npc:lady-sarevess","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","topic:naga","npc:gelihast","npc:lorgus-jett"},src={"Pool of Ask'ar"}}
E["zone:blackfathom"] = {t="dungeon",n="Blackfathom Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="Blackfathom Deeps is a flooded subterranean temple complex situated along the Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. Once a shrine dedicated to the night elven moon goddess Elune, the sunken sanctuary has been overtaken by the Twilight's Hammer cult, treacherous naga, and satyrs. They gather in its dark waters to venerate and nurture Aku'mai, a primordial pet and herald of the Old Gods.",h="Blackfathom Deeps is a flooded subterranean temple complex situated along the Zoram Strand in northwestern...",sec={{t="Sunken Sanctum of Elune",b="Long before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, this complex was known as Lathar'Lazal, a splendid temple dedicated to Elune. Highborne masons raised gem-encrusted bridges while Queen Azshara commanded the surrounding waters, partitionining salt seas and mountain streams around a sacred moonwell. When the Sundering tore the world apart ten thousand years ago, the temple sank into the coastal depths of the Veiled Sea. For millenia, it sat undisturbed beneath the waves—until foul whispers began seeping upward from the subterranean dark.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Ancient Horrors",b="Drawn by mad dreams and dark portents, the Twilight's Hammer cult converged on the sunken ruins. Within, they forged an unholy truce with coastal naga led by Lady Sarevess and prowling satyrs. Together, they desecrated the moonwell and enslaved local life. They drove the giant sea turtle Ghamoo-ra mad through years of torment, allowed the brutal murloc Gelihast to erect a blood shrine, and stocked cavernous depths with fresh sacrifices. Under the leadership of Twilight Lord Kelris, the cultists turned the ruins into a staging ground for the Old Gods' impending return.",sp=0},{t="The Slumbering Herald",b="At the deepest heart of the sunken temple lies Aku'mai, an ancient three-headed hydra carrying a spark of the Old Gods' primordial power. Twilight Lord Kelris believes this devourer is the herald of his dark masters and his personal ticket to immortality. Rather than a wild beast, the cult treats Aku'mai as a cherished divine pet, feeding her subjects and captives to nurture her strength. Striking down Kelris and extinguishing the cult's foul braziers breaks the wards binding her lair, allowing champions to slay the beast before its insatiable hunger is unleashed across Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Blackfathom Deeps before it fell into darkness?",a="Originally named Lathar'Lazal, it was a magnificent night elven temple dedicated to the moon goddess Elune. It featured crystal-clear pools, gemmed bridges, and a blessed moonwell, all overseen by Queen Azshara before the Great Sundering broke the temple and cast it beneath the sea.",al={"bfd history","who built bfd","original temple"},it="history"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer cultists here?",a="Drawn by nightmare visions and whispering voices from beneath Azeroth, the cultists came to worship the Old Gods. Under Twilight Lord Kelris, they took over the sunken ruins to nurture Aku'mai, offering living sacrifices in hopes of hastening the return of their chaotic masters.",al={"cultists in bfd","why is twilight's hammer here","what do cultists want"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris is the leader of the Twilight's Hammer cell within Blackfathom Deeps. Convinced that the awakening of Aku'mai will grant him eternal life and bring about the reign of the Old Gods, he orchestrates the cult's sacrifices and oversees the desecration of the temple.",al={"who is kelris","kelris lore","leader of bfd"},it="identity"},{q="What are the naga and satyr doing in the ruins?",a="Both the naga and satyrs were lured to the drowned temple by lingering ancient magical energies. The naga, led by Lady Sarevess, formed a pact with the Twilight's Hammer: the cultists feed her captives and dark knowledge, and in return, her sea witches provide magical shielding against the horrors lurking in the deep.",al={"why are naga here","why satyrs in bfd","lady sarevess"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Earthen Ring and Argent Dawn care about this place?",a="The Argent Dawn sent Scout Thaelrid to investigate suspicious alliances between the naga and cultists, uncovering proof of their murderous rituals. Meanwhile, the Earthen Ring rushed to Ashenvale because the invocation of Old Gods threatens the elemental balance and safety of the entire world.",al={"earthen ring ashenvale","argent dawn bfd","scout thaelrid"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Aku'mai is defeated?",a="Slaying Aku'mai severs the immediate physical foothold of the Old Gods within Ashenvale. It thwarts Twilight Lord Kelris's plot to unleash an ancient, flesh-devouring herald upon Kalimdor, striking a major blow against the Twilight's Hammer cult and cleansing a fragment of the dark taint infecting the ruined moonwell.",al={"what happens when you kill aku'mai","aku'mai ending","after killing final boss"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps is a sprawling, partially submerged subterranean cavern complex situated beneath the Zoram Strand along northwestern Ashenvale. Once an ancient night elven sanctuary known as Lathar'Lazal, its flooded passages and marble halls have been overrun by vile forces. Today, it serves as a corrupted subterranean stronghold where dark cultists, serpent naga, and twisted aquatic beasts gather around a shrine devoted to the chaotic Old Gods.",al={"what is bfd","what is blackfathom","about blackfathom deeps"},it="place",add=true,nx={8}},{q="Why is Blackfathom Deeps underwater?",a="Ten thousand years ago, the catastrophic Great Sundering tore ancient Kalimdor apart and shattered the surrounding coastline. The temple complex sank beneath the waters of the Veiled Sea as the land gave way. Over the millennia, the ocean swallowed most of its lower halls and courtyards, turning its majestic promenades into a flooded network of subterranean caves and tidal grottos.",al={"why is it flooded","why underwater bfd","how did it sink"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Who is Aku'Mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous, ancient three-headed hydra gifted with dark power, revered as a favored pet of the primordial Old Gods. Lurking in the deepest cavern of the ruins, this ancient beast possesses an insatiable hunger for living flesh and a mindless savagery that terrorizes the coastline. The Twilight's Hammer regards Aku'mai as a living harbinger of the Old Gods' ultimate return to Azeroth.",al={"who is akumai","what is akumai","hydra boss bfd"},it="threat",add=true,nx={10,11}},{q="Is Aku'Mai still alive down there?",a="Yes. Aku'mai dwells alive within its subterranean lair at the heart of the ruins. The Twilight's Hammer cultists actively supervise the monstrous hydra's growth, keeping it secluded and feeding it a steady stream of captured innocents and fallen subjects to satisfy its ferocious hunger until it is ready to unleash its full wrath.",al={"is akumai alive","is akumai asleep","is akumai still down there"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Who worships Aku'Mai?",a="Aku'mai is worshipped by the fanatical Twilight's Hammer cult, led within the ruins by Twilight Lord Kelris. They view the hydra as a sacred pet of their dark masters and a divine sign that the Old Gods will awaken. A tribe of local murlocs led by the vicious Gelihast also offers sacrifices to the presence within the deeps.",al={"who worships akumai","akumai worshippers","cultists worshipping akumai"},it="people",add=true},{q="Why does everyone seem so worried about this place?",a="Whenever the Old Gods are invoked, grave danger threatens all of Azeroth. Outside factions like the Argent Dawn and the Earthen Ring recognize that the gathering of cultists, naga, and satyrs under one dark banner portends catastrophic chaos. The cult's rituals, sacrifices, and nurturing of Aku'mai corrupt the surrounding waters and threaten to spread madness across Ashenvale.",al={"why worry bfd","why is blackfathom dangerous","threat of blackfathom"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Why are there naga and murlocs in the same ruins?",a="Both were drawn by the dark energies awakening within the ruins. The naga emerged from the sea to plumb the ancient power of the shattered temple and struck a sinister pact with the cult. Meanwhile, the murloc warrior Gelihast answered the call of the Old Gods, carving his way in and earning the cult's respect through raw brutality.",al={"why naga and murlocs","murlocs in bfd","naga in bfd"},it="threat",add=true},{q="Why me? Why send a stranger in instead of an army?",a="Marching an army into the sunken, flooded caverns is a logistical nightmare, and factions like the Argent Dawn operate quietly through scouts to avoid alerting the cult. Their covert scout, Thaelrid, was ambushed and mortally wounded within the halls. With time running out, they rely on capable, discreet champions like you to strike Kelris down before the cult's plans bear fruit.",al={"why send adventurers","why not send an army","why me bfd"},it="why_me",add=true},{q="If I kill Kelris, what happens next?",a="Kelris's death does not immediately clear the caverns. Defeating him leaves behind four ceremonial altar candles in his sanctum. Lighting these candles breaks the seals holding back the sanctuary's dark wards, triggering waves of cult defenders and opening the massive stone doorway that leads directly into Aku'mai's inner lair.",al={"after kelris is dead","kill kelris what happens","what happens when kelris dies"},sp=1,it="next_step",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="You followed rumors of ancient darkness to the misty Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. Hidden among the shoreline's ruins, a stair-lined shaft drops into the earth, forcing you to dive through flooded tunnels to reach these drowned halls. Whether dispatched by the night elves of Darnassus to find missing scouts, guided by the shaman of the Earthen Ring to investigate rising elemental corruption, or chasing whispers of the cultists amassing beneath the surf, your path led directly into the submerged sanctuary.",al={"how did i get here","how do i get in here","how did i find this place"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="You are here to purge the ancient temple of the evils festering within. The Twilight's Hammer cult, guided by Twilight Lord Kelris, has joined forces with local naga and satyrs to worship and feed the primordial beast Aku'mai. To stop their grim rituals, you must strike down the cultist leadership, put an end to the naga sorcery poisoning the waters, and venture into the lowest sanctum to slay the monstrous hydra before the herald of the Old Gods can unleash chaos upon Azeroth.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my goal here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the deeps represent a heartbreaking desecration of their heritage, as an ancient shrine of Elune and its sacred moonwell have been befouled by void cultists and monstrous aberrations.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman answering the call of Je'neu and the Earthen Ring must plunge into the watery dark to halt the corruption of the elements and banish the chaotic taint of the Old Gods.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Zoram'gar Outpost, the Horde seeks to secure the northern coast of Ashenvale from encroaching naga aggression and prevent the dark rituals within the deeps from threatening their outposts.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance heroes enter to rescue Scout Thaelrid, recover lost Highborne knowledge, and aid the night elves in cleansing their sacred homeland from cultist terror."},kw={"aku'mai","bfd","blackfathom","deeps","gelihast","ghamoo-ra","kelris","lathar'lazal","sarevess","zoram"},rel={"npc:aku-mai","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:lady-sarevess","npc:scout-thaelrid","quest:1200","quest:1199","quest:824","subzone:zoram-strand"},m={levels="24-32"},src={"Blackfathom Deeps (Classic)","Blackfathom Deeps"}}
